"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
10021,"(10021) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: In Thirty of the cows are sold, or sold, and forty are old."
10022,"(10022) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, who said: I was appointed to give alms from Akka, so I received There were scholars among those who ratified the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they disagreed over me. Some of them said, “Make it like He spoke the truth about camels, and among them were those who said, “There are thirty taba’a,” and among them were those who said, “There are forty cows.” An elderly cow."
10023,"(10023) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: In thirty tabi’a, or one jum’s ta’bi’a, or one jum’i. And forty women."
10024,"(10024) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If she reaches Thirty, then there is a taba’i’ in it, or a ta’bi’a, and if it reaches forty, then there is a musanna in it."
10025,"(10025) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He said: In thirty of the cows you sell one or two jadis, and in every forty there is a cow."
10026,"(10026) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Salih bin Dinar; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to Othman bin Muhammad bin Abi Suwayd: to take from all thirty villages by sale, And out of every forty cows, there was another cow, and nothing more than that."
10027,"(10027) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, and Hammad? They said: There are thirty jams, or two jams, and forty musannahs."
10028,"(10028) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr informed me, he said: Othman bin Al-Zubayr bin Abu Auf and others take one cow from every fifty."
10029,"(10029) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: When the cows reach thirty Then there is a taba' in it, or a jud'ah, or a jud'ah until it reaches forty, and when it reaches forty, then there is an old cow in it."
10030,"(10030) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban; That Naim bin Salamah informed him, and he was the one who had the seal of Omar bin Abdul Aziz in his hand: that Omar bin Abdul Aziz He called for a manuscript. They claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote it to Muadh. Na’im said: It was read while I was present. Then, behold, there is: out of every thirty tabi’a a jad’ah or two, and out of every forty heifers there is an old heifer. Na’im said: So I said: You are selling a trunk. Omar said: Rather, you are selling a trunk."
10031,"(10031) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: It is not There is nothing less than thirty cows."
10032,"(10032) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, he said: Not among less than thirty. Something cow."
10033,"(10033) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: Not There is something in it."
10034,"(10034) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Amr bin Marra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: There is nothing less than thirty cows."
10035,"(10035) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Mu’adh, So he ordered him to take some of the cows from every thirty tabi`a, or tabi`a, and from every forty musannah, so they asked him about What is the difference between them? He refused to take it until he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do not take anything. (Ahmad 5/2400 Malik 24)"
10036,"(10036) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Muadh, who said: There is nothing in the awqas."
10037,"(10037) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There is nothing wrong with hanging."
10038,"(10038) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: In forty years, and in Thirty sells, and nothing else."
10039,"(10039) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad, I said: What about fifty cows? The arbitrator said: There is a sin in it, and Hammad said: According to that."
10040,"(10040) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The owner of cows for more than the obligatory one."
10041,"(10041) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He did not increase So by calculation."
10042,"(10042) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: There is nothing in fudūl unless it is a composition."
10043,"(10043) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Al-Tabi’ is the one whose horns and ears have been made equal, and the elderly person: The second and upward."
10044,"(10044) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, he said: I said to Abu Qalaab: How much is Al-Sa’imah? He said: one hundred."
10045,"(10045) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no truth in any of the evil ones. Except for female camels, female cows and sheep."
10046,"(10046) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no The working cows are truthful."
10047,"(10047) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Muadh; He did not take zakat from working cows."
10048,"(10048) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: There is no truth in the herding cows."
10049,"(10049) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: There is no charity in working cows."
10050,"(10050) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubair said: There is no zakat on a two-tailed camel, nor on a working bull."
10051,"(10051) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: There is nothing in the factors of cows, except what is Traveling, and that is with camels."
10052,"(10052) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shehr, who said: There is no charity in working cows."
10053,"(10053) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no truthfulness in working cows."
10054,"(10054) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: The working cows are not responsible, nor are the camels. The one on which water is drawn and which one fights in the way of God as truthful."
10055,"(10055) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad told me that Abu al-Zubayr told him, about Jabir said: There is no truth in Al-Mathira."
10056,"(10056) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Does the burden and the thing that is raised contain the truth? He said: No, and Amr bin Dinar said: We heard that."
10057,"(10057) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He wrote The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the book of charity, so he tied it to his sword, or he said: by his will, and did not take it out to He worked for him until he was arrested, Abu Bakr worked for him until he died, and Omar worked for him: in the charity of sheep for every forty sheep. One sheep to twenty and one hundred, and if it exceeds two sheep to two hundred, and if it exceeds three to three hundred, then if it increases, then in Every hundred sheep is a sheep, and there is nothing in it until it reaches the hundred, and it should not be divided into a group, nor should it be combined. Separated, and if there are two mixtures, they come together as one."
10058,"(10058) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In every forty sheep One sheep up to twenty and a hundred, if more than that, then two sheep up to two hundred, if more than three sheep, up to three. Hundreds, and if there are many sheep, then for every hundred sheep there is a sheep."
10059,"(10059) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: For every forty sheep, there are up to twenty and a hundred sheep, If it adds one sheep, then it has two sheep to two hundred, and if it adds one sheep, then it has three sheep to three. A hundred sheep for every hundred sheep."
10060,"(10060) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Up to four hundred, if it is more than one. Up to five hundred, then on this account."
10061,"(10061) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In forty sheep, one to twenty and a hundred sheep, If it exceeds two hundred, then two sheep until it reaches two hundred, and if it exceeds two hundred, then three sheep until it reaches two hundred. It reaches three hundred."
10062,"(10062) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Ali, regarding the charity of sheep, he said: If it reaches forty, then there are two sheep up to one hundred and twenty sheep, and if it exceeds one, then there are two sheep up to two hundred sheep, then If it is increased by one, then it contains three sheep, up to three hundred. If it exceeds three hundred and becomes numerous, then in every hundred. A sheep, a shay, and Abdullah said, like what Ali said, until it reaches three hundred, then Abdullah said: If it is increased by one On three hundred, in it is four to four hundred, then on this account.
 Muhammad said: Amer told us, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: He does not unite what is separate, and he does not separate between a group."
10063,"(10063) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If she reaches forty, then there is tea in her until she reaches the age of Twenty and a hundred, if it increases one, then it has two to two hundred sheep, and if it increases one, then it has three sheep. Up to three hundred, and if it increases, then for every hundred there is one sheep, and the forty is omitted."
10064,"(10064) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When Omar sent the authenticator, he would send with him a letter: nothing in it was less than forty shekels."
10065,"(10065) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If not If you have anything but thirty-nine sheep, then there is no zakat on them."
10066,"(10066) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Not less than forty things."
10067,"(10067) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: It was the letter that Omar bin Abd wrote. Al-Aziz, when He sent them to give charity: There is no charity on sheep until they reach forty."
10068,"(10068) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no charity in anything less than forty."
10069,"(10069) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: There is nothing more than three hundred until you reach Four hundred."
10070,"(10070) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hamza, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: There is nothing more than three hundred, even It is four hundred, meaning sheep."
10071,"(10071) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: He wrote The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the book of charity, so he tied it to his sword, or he said: by his will, and he did not take it out to his workers. Until he was arrested, Abu Bakr worked on it until he died, then Omar worked on it, he said: In sheep, in three hundred sheep, three Sheeps, and if it is more, then for every hundred sheep there is a sheep, and there is nothing in it until it reaches the hundred."
10072,"(10072) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If it exceeds two hundred and one, then in it are three. One to three hundred sheep, and if it is more, then for every hundred sheep there is one sheep, and the forty is omitted."
10073,"(10073) Hatem bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If it exceeds three hundred, then for every hundred sheep there is a sheep."
10074,"(10074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who has forty sheep in Egypt that he milks, he said: He does not have to pay any zakat."
10075,"(10075) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no charity in the sheep of reared children."
10076,"(10076) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The khala is not to be considered. And it is not taken into account of charity."
10077,"(10077) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: Should the young children of the sheep be taken into account? He said: Yes."
10078,"(10078) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The child is to be counted when his mother gives birth to him."
10079,"(10079) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Bishr ibn Asim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar; He used to practice his father's practice of ta'if and its contraventions, and he used to give alms, so he used to treat them with food, so the people said to him: If you are willing to With food, he took some of it, and he withheld from them until he met Omar, and he informed him of what they said, and he said: Come back to them with food. And if the shepherd brings it, he will carry it in his hand, and tell them that you leave for them the master, the laborer, the cup, and the stallion. The sheep, and take the neck, the trunk, and the two, for that is fair between the choices of money and food."
10080,"(10080) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nas bin Qim, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Sufyan bin Abdullah, peace be upon him, for charity, and he said: Take what is between the food and the pyramid, meaning the food. Al-Sakhla."
10081,"(10081) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of a man from Thaqif, who said: I asked Abu Hurairah: What kind of money is given in charity? He said: In the middle third, so if the authenticator comes to you, bring out for him the jud` and the two."
10082,"(10082) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, or Shihab bin Malik, on the authority of Sa`id al-Araj, He said: I went out intending to wage jihad, so I met Omar in Mecca, and he said: With your companion’s permission, you went out? That is, Ali bin Umayyah. He said: I said: No. He said: Go back to your friend. When the man leaves his sheep for you, So they divided it into two parts, then they chose from the other half."
10083,"(10083) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard my father and others mentioning that Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz wrote: The sheep should be divided into thirds, then their master chooses a third, and the charity is taken from the middle third."
10084,"(10084) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: The sheep are divided into thirds."
10085,"(10085) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: When the authenticator comes, the sheep are divided. Three: one third is good, one third is evil, and one third is middle, and the certifier takes it from the middle."
10086,"(10086) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: The believer used to split the sheep in two parts. So the owner of the sheep chooses the better of the two."
10087,"(10087) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: He divides the sheep into two parts. The owner of the sheep chooses the better of the two parts, and the charity chooses from the other part."
10088,"(10088) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He gathers the thing, and the owner of the sheep takes a third of it. His choice, and the recipient of the charity takes from the two-thirds of his due."
10089,"(10089) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Two groups will separate."
10090,"(10090) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Like it."
10091,"(10091) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He wrote The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the book of charity, so he tied it to his sword, or he said: With his will, then he did not take it out to He worked on him until he died, and when he died, Abu Bakr worked on him until he died, then Omar worked on him: Charity is not to be taken as a pyramid. And not one with defects."
10092,"(10092) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: The believer is not taken. An old woman, an old woman, or a female goat, unless the approver so desires."
10093,"(10093) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Not for the believer. An old woman, nor a defective woman, nor a goat."
10094,"(10094) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The believer has neither an old woman nor a defective woman. There is no dispute unless the confirmer wills."
10095,"(10095) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I heard Suleiman bin Yassar, who said: It is not sufficient for charity. She is flawed."
10096,"(10096) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Maimun, who said: The weak and one-eyed ones are not to be taken for charity. Nor the barbarians, nor the lame women who do not follow the sheep."
10097,"(10097) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara, that His father, Yahya bin Amara, told him that Abu Sa`id used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no For anything less than five awsuqs, there is a sadaqah."
10098,"(10098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Not less than five. A handful of dates, and no raw grain. (Muslim 674. Ahmad 3/97)"
10099,"(10099) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no charity in anything less than five times."
10100,"(10100) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi (h) and on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said : There is no charity in anything less than five times. (Abdul Razzaq 7251. Ahmad 3/296)"
10101,"(10101) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the amount of food reaches five Awsq means charity."
10102,"(10102) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no truthfulness in anything less than five awsāq."
10103,"(10103) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Charity is not obligatory until It amounts to three hundred saa's."
10104,"(10104) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is nothing less than five awsuq’s."
10105,"(10105) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abi Saeed said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10106,"(10106) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10107,"(10107) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10108,"(10108) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10109,"(10109) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10110,"(10110) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’s."
10111,"(10111) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi (h) and on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir They said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10112,"(10112) Abd al-Rahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10113,"(10113) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10114,"(10114) Rawad bin Jarrah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10115,"(10115) Some of our companions told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yaqoub, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, He said: A wasq is sixty saa’."
10116,"(10116) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The tithe is for dates, raisins, wheat, and barley. (Daraqutni)"
10117,"(10117) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, on the authority of Musa bin Talha; When Muadh arrived in Yemen, he did not take zakat except from wheat, barley, dates, and raisins. (Ahmad 5/228 Daraqutni 8)"
10118,"(10118) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari; He only took wheat, barley, dates, and raisins."
10119,"(10119) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Truthfulness Of four: from wheat, and if there is no wheat, then dates, and if there are no dates, then raisins, and if there are no raisins So barley."
10120,"(10120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: Abd al-Hamid asked Musa ibn Talha about her? He said: The charity is only in wheat, barley, dates, and raisins."
10121,"(10121) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ataa said to me: There is no charity except for palm trees, or grapes, or Love, and Amr bin Dinar told me that."
10122,"(10122) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Zakat is on wheat, barley, dates, and raisins."
10123,"(10123) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqi told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: What the earth brought out was little of it, Or more than a tenth, or half a tenth."
10124,"(10124) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: For everything the earth paid a tenth, or half a tithe."
10125,"(10125) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In every matter, the earth comes out Zakat, even on ten days of harvest."
10126,"(10126) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he did not specify anything in the amount of fruit, and he said: The tenth. And half a tenth."
10127,"(10127) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid; Like him."
10128,"(10128) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote about that to the people of Yemen."
10129,"(10129) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In every matter the earth brought forth Zakat."
10130,"(10130) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is zakat on vegetables."
10131,"(10131) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: Not in Al-Khidr. Something."
10132,"(10132) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: It is not in legumes; Cucumbers, cucumbers, and the like are sadaqah."
10133,"(10133) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no charity in the harvest of the summer."
10134,"(10134) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: There is no zakat on vegetables, unless they become money. So it will be zakat."
10135,"(10134) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I heard Mujahid, and Ibrahim was sitting, saying: No. There is no zakat on legumes, apples, or vegetables."
10136,"(10136) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: There is no charity in vegetables."
10137,"(10137) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: I asked al-Hakam about the alfalfas and cottons, And sesame? He said: There is nothing in it. Al-Hakam said: What we have preserved from our companions is that they used to say: There is nothing in any of this, except in Wheat, barley, dates, and raisins."
10138,"(10138) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Khurasani, he said: There is no tithe on fruits; walnuts, Almonds, all legumes, and vegetables, but whatever is sold for two hundred dirhams or more is subject to zakat."
10139,"(10139) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: Not in legumes, reeds, and bread. And cucumbers, and celery, and fruits, and citron, and apples, and figs, and pomegranates, and persimmons, and fruits are counted as All of them are true."
10140,"(10140) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Ali bin al-Hakam, on the authority of Abi al-Ala bin al-Shakhir, he said: It is not There is no zakat on fodder or on legumes."
10141,"(10141) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning olives, he said: “The tenth is measured on them.”"
10142,"(10142) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: In olives, the tenth."
10143,"(10143) Zayd ibn Hubab told us, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Abi Salamah, who said: I asked Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir about Olive? He said: Omar bin Al-Khattab gave him tithes in the Levant."
10144,"(10144) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Raja’, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, who said: It contains the tenth."
10145,"(10145) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Sayyarih, he said: I said: : O Messenger of God, I have a bee. He said: Should I pay the tenth? I said: O Messenger of God, protect her for me. He said: So protect her for me. (Ahmad 2361, Ibn Majah 1823)"
10146,"(10146) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; The Emir of Taif wrote to Omar bin Al-Khattab: The people of honey have withheld from us what they used to give to those who were before us. He said: So he wrote If they give you what they used to give the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then protect it for them, otherwise do not protect it from them. He said: Amr bin Shuaib claimed that they used to give one sacrifice for every tithe. (Abu Dawud 1597)"
10147,"(10147) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Omar, who said: There is a tenth in honey."
10148,"(10148) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Munir bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Dhubab; He came to his people and said to them: There is zakat on honey, for there is no good in wealth that is not zakat. He said: They said: How much? Do you see? I said: The tenth. He said: So he took the tenth from them and brought it to Omar and told him what was in it. He said: So Omar took it and put it in it. Alms of Muslims."
10149,"(10149) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Concerning honey, the tenth."
10150,"(10150) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus; When Mu'adh came to Yemen, he brought honey and sheep's calves, and said: I was not ordered to do anything about them. (Abdul Razzaq 6944, Bayhaqi 128)"
10151,"(10151) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz Ali sent me Yemen, so I wanted to take a tenth of the honey. Mughirah ibn Hakim al-San’ani said: There is nothing in it, so I wrote to Omar. Ibn Abdul Aziz, and he said: He spoke the truth, and it was just and satisfied."
10152,"(10152) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Umar ibn Abdul Aziz asked me about his truthfulness. Honey? So I said: Al-Mughirah bin Hakim told me that there is no truth in it, and Omar said: He is just and confirmed."
10153,"(10153) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Adhiniya, who heard Ibn Abbas, who said: The amber is not a pile, but rather It is something that was swept away by the sea, and there is nothing in it."
10154,"(10154) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Adhiniya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Not in Amber is pure, but it is something washed away by the sea."
10155,"(10155) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is not in amber. Zakat, it is only spoils for the one who took it."
10156,"(10156) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar; Urwa bin Muhammad wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about a hangar containing seven hundred pounds. He said: In it The fifth."
10157,"(10157) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith; Omar bin Abdul Aziz is one-fifth of the amber."
10158,"(10158) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: In the fifth ward, and that was the case. He says about pearls."
10159,"(10159) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Ibrahim Ibn Saad asked Ibn Abbas about Amber? He said: If there is anything in it, then in it is one-fifth."
10160,"(10160) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; That Ibn Abbas was asked about amber? He said: If there is anything in it, then in it is one-fifth."
10161,"(10161) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan used to say: Not in amber, not in honey, not in acorns. Zakat."
10162,"(10162) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Not in the pearl stone, nor in the emerald stone. Zakat, unless they are for trade, and if they are for trade, then zakat is due on them."
10163,"(10163) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no zakat on beads and pearls, except that They are for trade."
10164,"(10164) A partner told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah; Like him."
10165,"(10165) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Not in beads and pearls. Zakat, unless it is for trade."
10166,"(10166) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, Al-Zuhri, and Makhul, they said: There is nothing in the jewels. Unless it is for business."
10167,"(10167) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He did not see zakat on jewellery, except for gold and silver, and he did not see zakat on jewels and pearls. And this is how."
10168,"(10168) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Everything with which I want to trade is in it. Zakat, even if it is milk or clay. He said: The referee was of the opinion that this was the case."
10169,"(10169) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no zakat on jewellery, unless it is bought. To trade."
10170,"(10170) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ata’ said to me: There is no charity in pearls, nor in aquamarines, nor in Rubies, cloves, turbans, or anything cannot be managed, and if any of that can be managed, then it is truthfulness. Its price when it is sold."
10171,"(10171) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Asama, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about pearls: Is there any zakat on it? He said: Any of it that is worn like jewelery is not for trade, so there is no zakat on it, and whatever of that is for trade. It is zakat."
10172,"(10172) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, in a hadith he mentioned; As if he sees zakat on it, meaning pearls."
10173,"(10173) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Whatever is irrigated in plain water, a tenth is in it, and whatever is irrigated in western waters It is half the tenth. (Daraqutni 7)"
10174,"(10174) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Yemen: It is taken from what the heavens watered, and it was irrigated with abundance of wheat, barley, dates, raisins, and what was irrigated. Half a tenth with a sawani."
10175,"(10175) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Muadh In Yemen, for as much as the heavens were watered, or a deer was irrigated, a tenth is given, and as for what was irrigated in the West and the Daliyah, half a tenth."
10176,"(10176) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enacted May God bless him and grant him peace, whether the heavens provided water, or the spring spring and the waters of the deer, or whether Baal was the full tithe, and he was not watered with bribes. So half a tenth."
10177,"(10177) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: While the heavens gave water Or it was sufficient, a tenth, and if it was irrigated with dalia, it is half a tenth."
10178,"(10178) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace As for what the heavens watered, or as the deer watered, Baal received a full tenth, and as for what was watered by bribes, it was half a tithe. He said: And his leaders said: And it was said: What is measured of the fruit is a tenth, or half a tenth. (Muslim 1571)"
10179,"(10179) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: The truth of the fruits, and the crops, and whatever is of palm trees, or crops of wheat, or barley, or basket of what Whether it is a raincoat, or it is irrigated by a river, or it is irrigated by a spring, or it is irrigated by rain, it contains a tenth, of each. One tenth, and whatever of it was irrigated with sprinklers is half a tenth, one for every twenty, and the Prophet wrote, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace to the people of Yemen, to Al-Harith bin Abd Kulal, and those with him from the people of Yemen from Ma’afir and Hamadan: The believers are due from the charity of their wealth a tithe, as much as the eye can satisfy, and as the heavens are satisfied, a tenth, and for what is irrigated in the West is half. The tithe. (Daraqutni 130, Bayhaqi 130)"
10180,"(10180) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: With regard to what is watered with thick palm trees, or Grapes, or grains, he said: the tenth."
10181,"(10181) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of Jabir, that he heard him say: It contains the tenth."
10182,"(10182) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: How many palm trees or stumps did Baal have? Love, or tillage? He said: The tenth. He said: So I said: How much is the amount of money used to irrigate a bush of palm trees, or grapes, or grains? He said: The tenth. I said: What about watering with buckets and basins? He said: Half a tenth."
10183,"(10183) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr informed me, he said: Jabir bin told me Abdullah; He said: Half a tenth."
10184,"(10184) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He did not specify anything with regard to the fruit, and he said: A tenth and a half-tenth."
10185,"(10185) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid; Like him."
10186,"(10186) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote about that to the people of Yemen."
10187,"(10187) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Concerning wheat, barley, dates, and grapes. If it is five awsqs, and that is three hundred saa’s, then in it is half a tenth, if it is to be watered, and the heavens and the eyes have not provided for it. So in it is the tenth."
10188,"(10188) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Nafi’; That Abdullah used to issue fatwas regarding the alms of crops and fruits. He would not drink from them in the river, or from springs, or Athriya, or Baal, then if you give him the tithe, one out of every ten, and whatever of it is watered with sprinkles, then if you give him the tithe Half of the tithes, and one for every twenty."
10189,"(10189) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; In the case of planting, it is in full bloom for a period of time, then it is watered with a well, meaning with a dahlia? He said: Most of this is given in charity if it is watered with it."
10190,"(10190) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: It will only be in the public eye for the general period of time, then He needs a well in the plot of water to water it, then the plot, then he goes to the spring. How did you believe him? He said: The tenth. He said: That would be more than that if he was irrigating with it, if he was irrigating with the eye more than If it is watered with a bucket more than what is watered with a straw, then it is half a tenth. I said: Is this also the case with money being a well, or a stumbling block of time, then it needs a well? He said: Yes. Abu Al-Zubayr said: I heard Ibn Umair say this, then I asked Salem bin Abdullah? He said: Like what Ubaid said."
10191,"(10191) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib al-Mu’allim, who said: Ata’ used to say: in the crops when its owner gives The reward of the reapers and those who scatter, is there any zakat on him for what he gave them? He said: No, the truth is about what happened to you."
10192,"(10192) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas; What about a man who spends on his fruit? One of them said: He pays zakat on it, and the other said: He raises the expenses and pays zakat on what is left."
10193,"(10193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Raise the seed, spend, and purify what He stayed."
10194,"(10194) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to seek charity, and he came to Al-Abbas to ask for his loan. Al-Abbas said to him: I put my wealth on loan for two years, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said: My uncle spoke the truth. (Tirmidhi 678 and Abu Dawud 1621)"
10195,"(10195) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdi, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in hastening it."
10196,"(10196) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in paying zakat in advance."
10197,"(10197) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, or on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in hastening. Zakat on your money, and you will be rewarded with it in the future."
10198,"(10198) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in paying the zakat in advance if he pays it. Everyone."
10199,"(10199) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Hafs ibn Sulaiman, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who brought Three years’ zakat multiplied? He said: It is sufficient."
10200,"(10200) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: There is no harm in hastening it before it is due."
10201,"(10201) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: No. It is unfortunate that he hastens it."
10202,"(10202) Omar bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He saw no harm in a man hastening his zakat before it was permissible."
10203,"(10203) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I do not know what this is, regarding hastening. Zakat one month or two months before it becomes lawful?"
10204,"(10204) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to bring food for himself from his land and pay zakat on it, then he would stay with him for two or three years, but he did not He purifies her, and he wants to sell it to her."
10205,"(10205) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya’, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Ja’far narrated to me; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: If a tenth is taken from the crop, there is no zakat on it, even if it remains for ten years."
10206,"(10206) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: When he brings out the zakat of crops, dates, and everything that grows, On the land, there is no zakat on it until one year has passed."
10207,"(10207) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: I want to eat food that I am holding, so he turns One year ago, he said: You are not obligated to give zakat in it, by my life. We will do that, we buy food, and we do not purify it. If you want to sell it, pay zakat on it if you sell it."
10208,"(10208) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Karim said to me in Al-Harith: If you give He paid his zakat the first time, but one year has passed since then, so do not pay zakat on it as it was the first time."
10209,"(10209) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; That Ali zakat the wealth of the Banu Abi Rafi’, orphans in his household, and said: Do you see that I have wealth that I cannot purify?!"
10210,"(10210) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: We were orphans in Aisha’s custody. She used to purify our wealth and throw it into the sea."
10211,"(10211) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: In the orphan’s wealth Zakat."
10212,"(10212) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to purify the orphan’s wealth."
10213,"(10213) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Omar said: Seek for the orphans Their wealth does not require zakat."
10214,"(10214) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya, Hanzali, and Hamid, on the authority of Al-Qasim; That Aisha used to scatter their money in the sea and pay zakat on it."
10215,"(10215) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar said: Seek money. Orphans, do not be deprived of charity."
10216,"(10216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is zakat on the orphan’s wealth."
10217,"(10217) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said regarding the orphan’s wealth: He has a right and he has a right upon him. I do not say anything except what God Almighty says."
10218,"(10218) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Yazid, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Give zakat the orphan’s wealth, otherwise it will be lost. A debt on your neck."
10219,"(10219) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: Ibn Umar was invited to a property. An orphan, and he said: If you wish, I will appoint him to purify him from year to year."
10220,"(10220) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Ata’; He saw zakat on the orphan’s wealth."
10221,"(10221) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; He used to say: Count the zakat that is due from the orphan’s wealth. When he reaches the age of maturity, inform him of it. If he wishes, he pays zakat on it, and if he wishes, he leaves it."
10222,"(10222) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no zakat on the orphan’s wealth until he reaches puberty."
10223,"(10223) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
10224,"(10224) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no zakat on the orphan’s wealth until he reaches puberty."
10225,"(10225) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He had property belonging to a brother’s son who had orphans, so he did not pay zakat on it."
10226,"(10226) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh, regarding the orphan’s wealth. He said: It is about to happen if you take from it. The animal and the two animals, nothing will remain of it."
10227,"(10227) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no zakat on the orphan’s wealth."
10228,"(10228) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Dinar, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about the orphan’s wealth, is there zakat on it? He said: Yes, even if I had it, I would not have purified it."
10229,"(10229) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Zaid, who said: I heard a mujahid saying: Count it, so if you know Fazzaqah."
10230,"(10230) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is taken from palm trees and livestock. Money until he has a wet dream. It means the orphan's property."
10231,"(10231) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim; Abu Wael said: There was in my custody an orphan who had eight thousand, but I did not purify her until when he reached the age of 10, I handed them over to him."
10232,"(10232) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: Ibn Umar had an orphan’s money. So he borrowed his money so that he would not pay his zakat."
10233,"(10233) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Khuthaym bin Arak, who said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no charity given to a Muslim regarding his slave or his horse. (Bukhari 1464, Muslim) 676)"
10234,"(10234) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Araak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “A Muslim does not have to do anything about his horse.” And his servant did not give charity. (Bukhari 1463 and Abu Dawud 1591)"
10235,"(10235) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Irrak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no zakat owed by a Muslim regarding his slave, nor his horse, nor his female child. (Daraqutni 8)"
10236,"(10236) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A Muslim does not have to do with his horse. And his servant did not give charity. (Tirmidhi 628 and Ahmad 2/477)"
10237,"(10237) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who narrated it, and said: I have overstepped your path. About the truthfulness of horses and slaves. (Ibn Majah 1813; Abu Ali 294)"
10238,"(10238) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: As for horses and slaves, I have pardoned their alms. (Ahmad 1/121)"
10239,"(10239) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Shubil bin Awf, who said: It was The pre-Islamic people realized that, and said: Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered the people to be truthful, and the people said: O Commander of the Faithful, a noble and gentle man for us. “Make ten days obligatory upon us.” He said: “As for me, I will not impose that upon you.”"
10240,"(10240) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Hussein informed me that Ibn Shihab He told him; That Othman used to ride horses, and that Al-Sa’ib, Nimr’s nephew, told him; He used to come to Omar with horses."
10241,"(10241) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The invading horse is not allowed to For the sake of God, truthfulness."
10242,"(10242) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: Ibn Al-Musayyab was asked: Is Al-Barathin truthful? He said: Or charity in horses."
10243,"(10243) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab on the authority of Al-Baradhin? He said to me: Is there charity in the horses? Or is there charity in horses?"
10244,"(10244) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Nafi’; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: There is no charity in horses."
10245,"(10245) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: There is no truth in horses or slaves."
10246,"(10246) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no charity in a wandering horse."
10247,"(10247) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about the charity of horses and slaves? He said: There is no zakat on it."
10248,"(10248) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He did not consider that slaves were to be traded as zakat al-fitr, but rather he would value them and pay zakat on their behalf."
10249,"(10249) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was saying that."
10250,"(10250) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no charity in horses, mice or donkeys."
10251,"(10251) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the slave for trade, he said: He does not have to pay zakat al-fitr."
10252,"(10252) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salim, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: He is not responsible for animals, nor is he against animals. Zakat, unless it is for trade."
10253,"(10253) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: There is no charity in horses. He said: Hammad is in it."
10254,"(10254) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about donkeys, is there a zakat on them or not? He said: As for me, I liken it to cows, and we do not know anything about it."
10255,"(10255) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no charity in donkeys."
10256,"(10256) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Two women came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in their hands were gold bracelets. The Messenger of God said to them: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Would you like for your Lord to surround you with bracelets of fire? They said: No, he said: So fulfill the right of this in your hands. (Ahmad 2/178 Daraqutni 108)"
10257,"(10257) Abd al-Rahim and Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musawar al-Warraq, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: Pass You asked the women of Muslims to give away their jewellery, and not to make gifts and extra money a loan between them."
10258,"(10258) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: He purifies his wife."
10259,"(10259) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad; He used to consider jewelry to be pure."
10260,"(10260) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is zakat on jewellery."
10261,"(10261) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed, who said: Zakat is given on jewellery."
10262,"(10262) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Concerning gold and silver jewellery. zakat He said: This is the saying of Sufyan."
10263,"(10263) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He used to command his wives to adorn their adornments."
10264,"(10264) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is zakat on jewellery."
10265,"(10265) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Zakat is given on jewellery."
10266,"(10266) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked: What about jewelry? Zakat? He said: Yes, if it is twenty mithqals, or two hundred dirhams."
10267,"(10267) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, Al-Zuhri, and Makhoul, who said: Zakat is given on jewellery."
10268,"(10268) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Fara’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: Concerning jewellery. Zakat, even on the ring."
10269,"(10269) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Maimun, who said: We had a collar which We had purified, until I see it has paid its price."
10270,"(10270) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the jewelry reaches a level where zakat is required, In it is zakat."
10271,"(10271) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not consider zakat on jewellery."
10272,"(10272) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan, and Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, He said: Our wealth was with Aisha, so she used to pay zakat on it except for jewellery."
10273,"(10273) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of A, on the authority of Aisha; She was not purified."
10274,"(10274) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dulham bin Salih, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Her brother’s daughters had jewels, so they did not Be pure"
10275,"(10275) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no zakat on Jewellery. I said: It contains a thousand dinars. He said: It is to be lent and worn."
10276,"(10276) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma; She did not purify her jewellery."
10277,"(10277) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’; She used to adorn her daughters with gold, but she did not purify it."
10278,"(10278) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I asked Omar about her zakat on jewellery? She said: I have not seen anyone purify me."
10279,"(10279) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: We do not know of any of the caliphs who said about jewelry. zakat"
10280,"(10280) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no zakat on jewellery, it is to be stripped and worn."
10281,"(10281) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Khlass, he said: There is no zakat on jewellery."
10282,"(10282) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn (h) and Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said : Zakat on bare jewellery."
10283,"(10283) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, who said: I heard Abu Ja`far say: It is not in jewelry. Zakat, then he recited: {And you extract from it ornaments that you wear}"
10284,"(10284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no zakat on jewellery."
10285,"(10285) Waki’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The zakat on jewelery is to be loaned and worn."
10286,"(10286) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amara, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amriya, who said: We were We were orphans in Aisha’s care, and we had some jewellery, but she did not pay zakat on them."
10287,"(10287) Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Saad, Ibn Umar, and Abu Hurairah, And Abu Saeed, I said: I have money, and I want to give it zakat, but I cannot find a place for it, and these people are making What do you see? He said: They all ordered me to give it to them."
10288,"(10288) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar said: Pay the zakat on your wealth to whomever And God has commanded you, so whoever is righteous, it is for his own soul, and whoever is unrighteous, it is for himself."
10289,"(10289) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, he said: Riyah bin Ubaidah narrated to me, on the authority of Qaz’a, He said: I said to Ibn Omar: I have money, so to whom should I pay its zakat? He said: Give it to these people, meaning the princes. I said: Then they take with it clothing and perfume. He said: And if they take Clothes and perfumes, but there is no right to anything other than zakat, O Qaz’a."
10290,"(10290) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hajib ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, who said: I asked Ibn Umar? So he said: Give it to them, and if they eat dog meat with it, then when they returned to him, he said: Give it to them."
10291,"(10291) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Mujalid; Did you ask Ibn Omar about her? He said: Give it to them, even if they eat it."
10292,"(10292) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shuabi; He used to send his charity to the princes."
10293,"(10293) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Hudhayf and Sa`id Bin Umair wanted the zakat to be paid to the Sultan."
10294,"(10294) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Charity was given to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And whoever commanded it, and to Abu Bakr and whoever commanded it, and to Omar and whoever commanded it, and to Uthman and whoever commanded it, and when he was killed Othman disagreed, some of them thought that he should give it to them, and some of them thought that he should divide it with him. Muhammad said: Let whoever chooses to divide it with him fear God, and let him not find fault with them in the least. He comes like The one who reproaches them."
10295,"(10295) Abdou told us, on the authority of Harithah bin Abi Al-Rijal, he said: I asked Omar about zakat? She said: Aisha said: Give her to those in authority among you."
10296,"(10296) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, he said: I asked Abu Ja`far about zakat. Should I pay it to him? Governor? He said: Give it to them."
10297,"(10297) Abdou told us, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Four to the Sultan; Prayer, zakat, punishments, and making up."
10298,"(10298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He included, or within, these people were four; Prayer, zakat, punishments, and wisdom."
10299,"(10299) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that he was asked about zakat? He said: Give it to the Sultan, and it was said: They do it and they do it, twice. He said: So you can Do you place them in their proper places? They said: No, he said: So give it to them."
10300,"(10300) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Khathami, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Give her the princes. What they prayed He said: And Khaythama said: They did not perform the prayer at its proper time."
10301,"(10301) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Kulthum bin Jabr, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, that he said: {And perform the prayer and pay the poor-rate} He said: This is an obligation for the Sultan."
10302,"(10302) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He was of the opinion that zakat should be paid to the Sultan."
10303,"(10303) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Bilamani, He said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said regarding Omar’s bequests: Whoever pays zakat to someone other than his guardian, it will not be accepted from him, even if his charity Give alms for the whole world."
10304,"(10304) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: Give the zakat of your money to the Sultan."
10305,"(10305) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Al-Daylam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira and Ibn Umar said: Pay the zakat on your money to the Sultan."
10306,"(10306) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Numan, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A man asked him about zakat? He said: Give it to the imam. He said: The imam is the Qur’an, and he was hiding that."
10307,"(10307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Hasan. They said: Put them in their proper places. And he hid it."
10308,"(10308) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Utba al-Kindi, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Put it among the poor."
10309,"(10309) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Yahya, who said: A man asked Saeed bin Jubayr about Honesty? He said: To the ruler of the matter. He said: Al-Hajjaj builds palaces with it, and places them in places other than their proper places. He said: Place them where you were commanded for them to be."
10310,"(10310) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he gives it to them, it will be sufficient for him, and if he divides it, It suffices."
10311,"(10311) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about zakat? He said: Give it to them. Then I asked him after, and he said: Do not give it to them, for they have missed the prayer."
10312,"(10312) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man brought the zakat of his wealth to Ali, and he said Ali: Will you take something from our giving? He said: No. He said: We do not agree that we should not give to you and take from you. So he ordered him to divide it."
10313,"(10313) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said:"
10314,"(10314) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no zakat on any property, until it is transferred to it. squint"
10315,"(10315) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no zakat on wealth. Until a year passes over him."
10316,"(10316) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever acquires money, does not Zakat is due on him until one year has passed."
10317,"(10317) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who said: It is not upon him. Zakat until one year has passed."
10318,"(10318) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: Any man who gives money does not Zakat on him, until one year has passed."
10319,"(10319) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salem, who said: There is no zakat on it even. The year will pass over him."
10320,"(10320) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no zakat on any property, until it is transferred to it. squint"
10321,"(10321) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, or others, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no zakat on it until The year will pass over him."
10322,"(10322) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Harithah ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, she said: No. Zakat on wealth until one year has passed."
10323,"(10323) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: There is no zakat on it. Until a year passes over him."
10324,"(10324) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ali bin Numan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: He does not have to pay zakat until one year has passed from him, from when he benefits from it."
10325,"(10325) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a man has a month to pay zakat on it and he acquires money So he spends on it, then he does not have to pay zakat on what he spent, but if he completes the month in which he pays zakat on his wealth, then If he does not have a month to pay zakat on and he has benefited from money, then let him pay zakat on it when he benefits from it."
10326,"(10326) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; What about a man who benefits from money? He said: He purifies it when it benefits you."
10327,"(10327) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to say: If a man benefits from money and wants to spend it before the month of zakat comes, let him pay it, then To spend on it, and if he does not want to spend, then to pay zakat on it along with his wealth."
10328,"(10328) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no zakat on the wealth of the offices."
10329,"(10329) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: There is no zakat on the wealth of the offices."
10330,"(10330) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Subayh Abi al-Jahm, the mawla of Banu Abs, who said: I asked Sa`id bin Jubayr and Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man who is a correspondent and has wealth, is the highest zakat on his wealth? They said: No."
10331,"(10331) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Abu Maimun ibn Mihran, on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of Stolen, he said: There is no zakat on the wealth of the offices."
10332,"(10332) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is not in the offices’ money. And the servant does not pay zakat until he is freed."
10333,"(10333) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is not in the wealth of the offices, nor is the slave. zakat"
10334,"(10334) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Sakhr, on the authority of Kaysan Abi Sa’id. Al-Maqbari, he said: I brought my zakat to Omar, two hundred dirhams, and I am writing. He said: Have you been freed? I said: Yes, he said: Go and divide it."
10335,"(10335) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa; Like Jabir said."
10336,"(10336) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It is not in the slave’s wealth. zakat"
10337,"(10337) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, who said: There is no zakat on the slave’s wealth."
10338,"(10338) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: It is not in the slave’s wealth. zakat"
10339,"(10339) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The slave and his property are the property of his master, the zakat is due on the master. There is no zakat due on the servant."
10340,"(10340) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not Zakat is given on the slave’s wealth."
10341,"(10341) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is not in the slave’s wealth. zakat"
10342,"(10342) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I do not have to The servant is paid zakat."
10343,"(10343) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah; He was asked about the servant: Does he owe zakat? He said: May peace be upon him?"
10344,"(10344) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Zakat is given to the slave’s wealth."
10345,"(10345) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Jabir al-Hadha’, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Is there money? Is zakat due on the slave? He said: Muslim? I said: Yes, he said: In two hundred dirhams, five dirhams."
10346,"(10346) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: Ali was asked about a man who has a debt owed by another man? He said: The owner of the money pays zakat on it. If he repents of what he owes and is afraid that he will not pay it off, then he gives it a respite. He paid his past zakat."
10347,"(10347) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I was informed that Ali said: If he is truthful, then may he pay zakat. Receipt, meaning the debt."
10348,"(10348) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If you have a debt, pay it off."
10349,"(10349) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: To see what debt he had owed. Let him isolate him, and whoever has a trustworthy debtor, let him purify him, and whoever is not settled, let him give him this day and take it. For two days, let him purify him."
10350,"(10350) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He purifies you."
10351,"(10351) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The zakat on your wealth is about Until a year, then pay zakat on whatever debt is trustworthy, and whatever debt is doubtful, pay zakat on it until it is paid off. His companion"
10352,"(10352) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He purifies you."
10353,"(10353) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir; That Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr informed him that Omar said to a man: When it is permissible, calculate your debt and what you have, then collect that. All together, then purify it."
10354,"(10354) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: Whatever religion you do not hope for, consider it. Then pay what you owe, then pay zakat on what remains."
10355,"(10355) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you knew that he was going out Fazakah"
10356,"(10356) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: Ali was asked about If a man has debts and doubts, are they pure? He said: If he is truthful, then he will pay zakat on him for what has passed, if he takes possession of him."
10357,"(10357) Hammad bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Uthman, who said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: We have a loan and a loan and a debt, so shall we purify it? He said: Yes, Aisha used to command us to purify what is in the sea. I asked Salem? He said: Like that."
10358,"(10358) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no zakat on the debt."
10359,"(10359) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mu’mil, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, on the authority of Aisha, she said: There is no zakat on it until he takes possession of it."
10360,"(10360) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He does not pay zakat until He grasps it."
10361,"(10361) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The owner of the debt is not responsible for what he owes, nor for what he owes. He is the one who pays zakat."
10362,"(10362) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no zakat on it even. He grasps it."
10363,"(10363) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Abraham disagreed with me about it, so I said: He will not pay zakat on you, then he returned. To what you said."
10364,"(10364) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: There is no zakat on the debt."
10365,"(10365) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in the servant being repaid. his companions, and to give alms from the bounty as well."
10366,"(10366) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The servant gives something in charity from his sustenance and it will not be harmed. With it"
10367,"(10367) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; A man asked him, and he said: I am a wealthy man and I have money, so should I give him alms? He said: Yes, for three dirhams, four dirhams."
10368,"(10368) Yahya bin Zakariyya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: What Does the servant give some of his wealth in charity? He said: The Saa’ and the like."
10369,"(10369) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The servant gives in charity something less than a dirham."
10370,"(10370) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, and it was Owned by Banu Hashim; He asked Omar, “Do you give charity?” He said: With dirhams and a loaf of bread."
10371,"(10371) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, on the authority of Salim, who said: He seeks closeness with whatever goodness he is able."
10372,"(10372) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Khaythamiyah; Does the servant give alms? They said: He should not give in charity more than a dirham."
10373,"(10373) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: He gives something in charity, not of a waste."
10374,"(10374) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Umar, the servant of Abi al-Lahm, who said: I was a slave owned, and I was... Do you give charity? I asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was my master. He disavowed me, or he asked him, and he said: The reward is between you. (Muslim 711. Ibn Majah 2297)"
10375,"(10375) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: He gives dirhams in charity."
10376,"(10376) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He answers the call of the slaves. (Ibn Saad 370)"
10377,"(10377) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to answer prayers. The owned ones (Tirmidhi 1017 and Ibn Majah 4178)"
10378,"(10378) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Salman, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He does not give in charity. The slave has responsibility over his father, or over his mother, except with the permission of his master."
10379,"(10379) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Dirham, who said: I asked Abu Huraira, I said: He has made My master owes me a dirham today, should I give it in charity? He said: It is not permissible for you to take any of your blood or any of your property except with His permission. You should give a morsel to the poor."
10380,"(10380) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The servant does not give any of his money in charity, except With the permission of his master."
10381,"(10381) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sulaiman, who said: I witnessed Al-Sha’bi, and Mamluk asked him, and he said: I I earned such-and-such, and my master takes such-and-such, so should I give in charity? He said: Then the reward will be for your masters."
10382,"(10382) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad; Amr ibn al-Aas used to order something to be given to the poor, and if there was no need for someone else to give it to him."
10383,"(10383) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; He dislikes it when a beggar is ordered to eat food and he is not able to eat it until he gives it in charity."
10384,"(10384) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khabab bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed; That a questioner asked Humaid bin Abdul Rahman? So Hamid said to him: You are lost, as if he were my servants. So he commanded him to do something and he took it away and refused to accept it, so he said Praise be to Him: Whatever you wish if you accept it, otherwise We will give it to someone else. Then he said: It used to be said: Return the questioner, even if it is for the equivalent of a head. The cat"
10385,"(10385) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who gives charity to the beggar and then he leaves it and does not find it? He said: He can change it to something else."
10386,"(10386) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who gives zakat to the poor and they miss it. He said: He withholds it until he gives her another poor person. He does not go back on anything that he has made for God."
10387,"(10387) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Concerning the questioner, if he goes out to him with a broken piece and does not find it, lock it up until someone else comes."
10388,"(10388) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Al-Aas used to say: When he came out to him with a kasra But he was not found, so they imprisoned her until someone else came."
10389,"(10389) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, who said: He places it Until someone else comes."
10390,"(10390) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: He keeps her imprisoned until he gives her to someone else."
10391,"(10391) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He can do with it whatever he wants."
10392,"(10392) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Amir, and Ata’, they said: If he wishes, he can spend it. And if He willed, He could keep it."
10393,"(10393) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas and al-Hasan. They said: What was taken from you, Ali. Bridges and bridges, this is zakat for the past."
10394,"(10394) Abu Al-Ahwas and Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Account for what was taken from you. Tax collectors from your property’s zakat."
10395,"(10395) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I asked Abu Razin: What does the tax collector take from the merchants? He said: He counts with it from his zakat."
10396,"(10396) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Hasan, who said: He did not take the tenth from you. So count with it as zakat."
10397,"(10397) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will be rewarded with it."
10398,"(10398) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he passes by the tenth and takes from him, he will be counted with it from Zakat"
10399,"(10399) Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abd Allah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Concerning a man passing by the tenth So it will be taken from him? He said: He will take account of what they took from him from the zakat of his wealth."
10400,"(10400) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He will be rewarded with it."
10401,"(10401) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked him? He said: Be rewarded with what was taken from you on the tenth."
10402,"(10402) Muhammad Ibn Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abi Qalabi, he said: Do not be rewarded with what He took the tenth from you."
10403,"(10403) Omar bin Ayyub al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimoon, who said: He is not to be counted in it."
10404,"(10404) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Tawus who said: Do not think about what was taken from you. The tenth"
10405,"(10405) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwair, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He is not counted for it."
10406,"(10406) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Sudair, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Do not be rewarded for what the tenth was taken from you."
10407,"(10407) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and on the authority of Hisham, or someone else, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They both hated that zakat should be paid from one country to another."
10408,"(10408) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked that charity be carried from one country to another."
10409,"(10409) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad; Omar bin Abdul Aziz was sent to him with zakat from Iraq to the Levant, and he returned it to Iraq."
10410,"(10410) Had Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Murrah, who said: Did you ask your wife Al-Qasim? She said: We have collected some dirhams from our zakat, so I sent them to the Levant, and he said: Give them to the prince in Medina."
10411,"(10411) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Layna, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Put the zakat on the town you are in. If there are no poor people there, then to the one next to it."
10412,"(10412) Abu Khalid narrated to us, not by Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Farqad Al-Sabkhi, who said: He was sent with me to pay zakat. To Mecca, I met Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: Return her to the land from which I carried her."
10413,"(10413) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khaldi, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; He sent his wealth to Medina with his alms."
10414,"(10414) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sasan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Come to the Muslims, so give him. Wherever you want."
10415,"(10415) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimoon, who said: He preferred to be sent with truthfulness to The children of the Muhajireen and Ansar in Medina."
10416,"(10416) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Tawoos used to see that the dissenter would sit, and if he was given something, he would take it. And if he is not given anything, he remains silent."
10417,"(10417) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban; One of the bravest of his informants was that two sheikhs reported that Muhammad bin Muslimah Al-Ansari, one of the companions of Badr, had come to them. So he gave their livestock in charity in the time of Omar ibn al-Khattab, and he used to sit, so whoever brought him a sheep in it would fulfill his right. He accepted it from him."
10418,"(10418) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Haritha, he said: We sent Umar as confirmers, So, when we are given anything in it, it is a fulfillment of our right, we accept it from him."
10419,"(10419) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The one who confirms Their vows, and he does not make them swear to you."
10420,"(10420) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The confirmator used to come. He saw camels and sheep standing and believed them, but did not wait."
10421,"(10421) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded By paying zakat al-fitr before prayer. (Bukhari 1509. Muslim 679)"
10422,"(10422) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to take it out before praying."
10423,"(10423) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar (h) and on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Like him"
10424,"(10424) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Sunnah is to go out. Sadaqat al-Fitr before the prayer. (Daraqutni 70)"
10425,"(10425) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He loved to pay the zakat al-fitr before he went out to the grave."
10426,"(10426) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; He used to give the zakat al-fitr before the prayer."
10427,"(10427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He used to take it out before prayer."
10428,"(10428) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, who said: Abu Nadhri used to sit on the Day of Fitr in The mosque of the neighborhood, so he gives their zakat and sends it among those who remain, so he gives his zakat and divides it among the poor of the neighborhood Then he comes out."
10429,"(10429) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: A man should not go out on the Day of Breakfast to The person praying, until he pays the alms of al-Fitr, and what his family owes."
10430,"(10430) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Give your zakat before your prayer."
10431,"(10431) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: They used to prefer giving it out before prayer."
10432,"(10432) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to give the zakat al-fitr after the prayer."
10433,"(10433) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: Mujahid’s circumcision told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: He spoke the truth. Breaking the fast on the day of breaking the fast is zakat, and whoever gives it after that, it is zakat."
10434,"(10434) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Misra used to feed food after He prays."
10435,"(10435) Saul bin Yusuf and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is obligatory. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, granted the breaking of the fast to every free man or slave, young or old, male or female. A female, a saa’ of dates, or barley, or half a saa’ of wheat. (Abu Dawud 1619. An-Nasa’i 2287)"
10436,"(10436) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Uthman, who said: A saa’ of dates, or half A saa of wheat."
10437,"(10437) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab, he said: Tell me who brought the truth to al-Fitr to Abu Bakr. Half a saa' of food."
10438,"(10438) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he narrates it; He was asked about the truthfulness of breaking the fast? He said: On behalf of the young, the old, the free, and the owned, half a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of dates, or barley."
10439,"(10439) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He told the truth about breaking the fast on the authority of the young, the old, and the free. And the slave, for every human being, is half a saa’ of wheat."
10440,"(10440) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: For every person, half a saa’ of wheat, and whoever is against wheat, from Dates, or raisins, or acorns, or barley, or something else, is a complete saa’."
10441,"(10441) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He used to say: He broke the fast on behalf of the free people who fasted, and on behalf of the slaves who fasted, and on behalf of the slaves who did not fast, half a saa’ of wheat. Or a saa of dates, or barley."
10442,"(10442) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said something similar to what Al-Sha’bi said about free people who did not fast."
10443,"(10443) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya and Al-Aswad, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: two muddans of wheat, or a saa’ of dates, or barley."
10444,"(10444) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; Like him"
10445,"(10445) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Half a saa' of wheat, or a saa' of dates."
10446,"(10446) Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He said: a saa of dates, or a saa of barley."
10447,"(10447) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A muddan of wheat, or a saa’ of dates, or Barley"
10448,"(10448) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr; He heard Ibn Al-Zubair, while he was on the pulpit, saying: A muddan of wheat, or a saa’ of barley, or dates."
10449,"(10449) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of his people; He asked Al-Hakam, and Hammad? They said: Half a Saa' of wheat. He said: And I asked Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim and Saad bin Ibrahim? They said like that."
10450,"(10450) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Sulaiman Al-Shaybani, he said: Abu Habib told me, he said: I asked Abdul Allah Ibn Shaddad about Sadaqah al-Fitr? He said: Half a saa' of wheat, or flour."
10451,"(10451) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Ali; The zakat for breaking the fast is a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley, or half a saa’ of wheat."
10452,"(10452) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’; She used to give zakat al-fitr on behalf of whomever she provided from among her family, whether present or absent, half a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of dates. Or barley."
10453,"(10453) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: I heard the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz to Adi being read with sight. In the month of Ramadan: for every person, young or old, free or slave, male or female, half a saa’ of wheat, or a saa’ of wheat. From dates"
10454,"(10454) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Sadaqah is a saa’ of dates, or Half a saa' of food."
10455,"(10455) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed He, peace and blessings be upon him, gave zakat al-fitr, a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of barley. He said: Ibn Umar used to give it to him on behalf of his wives, and the mamluks of his wives, except for two servants who were appointed. He did not give on their behalf. (Bukhari 1503, Muslim 12)"
10456,"(10456) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it obligatory He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, gave the al-Fitr charity: a saa of dates, or a saa of barley, for every slave, or free man, young or old. (Bukhari 1512 and Abu Dawud 1609)"
10457,"(10457) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Sarh, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri; Concerning Al-Fitr, he said: By God, I will not go out except as long as we used to go out at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a saa’. Of dates, or a saa of barley, or a saa of raisins, or a saa of aqat. (Bukhari 1506, Abu Dawud 1612)"
10458,"(10458) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: What is most beloved to me is that when God expands People must complete a saa’ of wheat for each person."
10459,"(10459) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: For every person, a saa’ of wheat is given as zakat al-fitr."
10460,"(10460) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Masruq saying: The zakat al-fitr: a saa’, a saa’."
10461,"(10461) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman say: A saa’, a saa’, on the authority of Every little thing and every great thing is written."
10462,"(10462) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to us: {What an evil name? Immorality after faith} Sadaqah al-Fitr: a saa’, a saa’."
10463,"(10463) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, who said: The truth of breaking the fast on behalf of the young and the old, And the free, and the slave, and the male, and the female. He said: If they give to the extent that they give to the point of conception."
10464,"(10464) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Abi Al-Aaliyyah, and Ibn Sirin. They said: Sadaqat al-Fitr on the authority of The young, the old, the free, the slave, the witness, the absent, the male, the female, the rich, and the poor."
10465,"(10465) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: This is upon the one who is able to fast."
10466,"(10466) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: He spoke the truth. Break the fast upon whomever you spend your expenses upon."
10467,"(10467) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to prefer dates in his zakat al-fitr."
10468,"(10468) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The alms of mushrooms are sufficient for wheat. And barley, and dates, and raisins, and salt, and he doubted the flour and the stalk, and said: Of all of these is equal."
10469,"(10469) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, who said: I heard the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz being read to Adi in Basra: Half a dirham will be taken from the people of the Diwan from their gifts, for each person."
10470,"(10470) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: We received the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz regarding zakat al-fitr: half a saa’ on the authority of Each person, or his value, is half a dirham."
10471,"(10471) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in giving dirhams in charity. Breakfast"
10472,"(10472) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq say: I caught them while they were giving in Ramadan charity, dirhams for the value of food."
10473,"(10473) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He hated to be given a paper in his zakat al-fitr."
10474,"(10474) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: I heard him say: The Muslim man pays zakat al-fitr on behalf of his Christian slaves."
10475,"(10475) Abdullah bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn Umar that he used to give The Christian slaves are sincere and fitrah."
10476,"(10476) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: He wrote to Ata’ asking him about Ubaid. Jews and Christians, should I pay zakat al-fitr on their behalf? He said: Yes."
10477,"(10477) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said the same as Omar bin Abdul Aziz said."
10478,"(10478) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: If you have Christian slaves, they will not be ignored. It means for trade, so redeem them on the Day of Fitr."
10479,"(10479) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar used to give charity on behalf of his servants in the land of Omar."
10480,"(10480) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’; She used to give zakat al-fitr on behalf of whomever she wanted from her family. The witness and the absent."
10481,"(10481) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd Al-Rahman, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, Ata’ bin Yasar, and Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, they said: He who has a slave in A crop, or an udder, so he has to pay zakat al-fitr."
10482,"(10482) It was narrated on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Nafi’ narrated to me; That Abdullah bin Omar used to pay zakat al-fitr on behalf of his entire household; Free them and their slave, young and old, Muslim and unbelieving slaves."
10483,"(10483) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to give on behalf of the workers of his land."
10484,"(10484) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Give zakat to the slave of livestock or tillage. ? He said: No."
10485,"(10485) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, Al-Sha’bi, and Ibn Sirin. They said: He is the witness. And the absent one."
10486,"(10486) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Umayyah ibn Abi Uthman informed me, on the authority of Umayyah ibn Abdullah; Nafi’ ibn Alqamah wrote to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan asking him about the slave in the wall and the livestock, upon him. Zakat on the day of Fitr? He said: No, because you only gave zakat on the wall and the cattle that are in it, so there is no zakat on it."
10487,"(10487) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, ibn Umar, who said: He had two offices, but he did not give About them"
10488,"(10488) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to see the truth about Ramadan."
10489,"(10489) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I was informed that Maimun was performing The deeds are the truth of nature."
10490,"(10490) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If it was written and subtracted from itself, then it is It is enough for himself, and if he does not leave it for himself, then he should feed his master on his behalf."
10491,"(10491) Ibn al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was not obligated to pay zakat al-fitr."
10492,"(10492) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He gives each people the equivalent of the share of the people of Medina."
10493,"(10493) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: With the tide with which you gain sustenance. destroy you"
10494,"(10494) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: Salem used to pay the zakat al-fitr with a saa’ of zakat al-fitr. The market that day before dawn, and nothing will come out except dates."
10495,"(10495) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Each people is given according to their share."
10496,"(10496) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, or on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa, she said: With the tide and the saa with which they differ."
10497,"(10497) Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you give according to the extension of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, it will be sufficient. On your behalf, and if you give the food with which you support your family, it will be sufficient for you."
10498,"(10498) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: I would love for you to give with your measure today. With a measure that you can take and feed yourself with."
10499,"(10499) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not give charity except to your people of religion, so God Almighty revealed: {It is not upon you to give them their gifts}, to His saying: {And whatever good you spend, it will be repaid to you in full}. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give alms to the people of Religions (Nasa’i 11052. Hakim 285)"
10500,"(10500) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Salem al-Makki, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: People hate that They gave alms to the polytheists, so God Almighty revealed: {It is not upon you to guide them}, saying: So the people gave alms to them."
10501,"(10501) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not give alms to a Jew or a Christian unless you find Change it"
10502,"(10502) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I was with Shaqiq ibn Salamah, and he passed by He took over my captives from the polytheists, so he commanded me to give alms to them. Then he recited these verses: {And they give food according to their love. The poor, the orphan, and the prisoner}."
10503,"(10503) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Feed him, but do not give him Your expenses"
10504,"(10504) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra; He used to give the monks some of his zakat al-fitr."
10505,"(10505) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Do not give charity to me. The Jew and the Christian at your expense."
10506,"(10506) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of giving; {And they give food for the love of it to the poor, the orphan, and the captive.} They said: from the people of the tribe and others."
10507,"(10507) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Absi, on the authority of Omar; In the Almighty’s saying: {The alms are only for the poor}, He said: They are the time of the People of the Book."
10508,"(10508) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawus; They hated giving charity to Christians."
10509,"(10509) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Batti, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the words of God Almighty: {And they feed food, despite the love of Him, to the needy and the orphan and the captive} He said: The captives are from the people of polytheism."
10510,"(10510) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Abi Habib informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, on the authority of Jabir. Ibn Zaid, he said: He was asked about whom should charity be attributed to? He said: Concerning the Muslims and the people of your protection, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was The zakat and the fifth are distributed among the people of Dhimmah. (Abu Ubaid 1992, Ibn Zanjoyah 2291)"
10511,"(10511) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, who said: I asked Ibrahim about telling the truth to people other than his family. Islam? He said: As for zakat, no, but if a man wants to give in charity, there is no problem."
10512,"(10512) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Do not give them zakat. And give them what you do voluntarily."
10513,"(10513) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It will not be given to him. The polytheists receive some zakat."
10514,"(10514) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, who said: Do not give the Jews Christians are part of zakat, and there is no harm in giving alms to them."
10515,"(10515) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The polytheists are not given zakat, nor Something of the expiations."
10516,"(10516) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He is given from the zakat to whomever has it. The house, the servant, and the horse."
10517,"(10517) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They did not withhold zakat from the owner of the household or the servant."
10518,"(10518) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He did not see any harm in Some of it will be given to someone who has a servant and a home, if he is in need."
10519,"(10519) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I asked Muqatil bin Hayyan about a man in The courtier has a gift and a horse, and he is in need. Should I give him zakat? He said: Yes."
10520,"(10520) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to buy a slave from the zakat of his wealth to free her."
10521,"(10521) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to buy a slave from zakat and free her."
10522,"(10522) A partner told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; He hated to buy a slave from zakat and free her."
10523,"(10523) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Huraim and Ja’far Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr said: Do not be freed from zakat. Jafar added: fear of dragging loyalty."
10524,"(10524) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who bought his father’s property from the zakat and then freed him? He said: Buy the best slaves."
10525,"(10525) Abu Ja’far told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He did not see any harm in a man giving zakat during Hajj or freeing a woman from it."
10526,"(10526) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: Omar said: If you give, then enrich. It means: from charity."
10527,"(10527) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to give from Zakat is not capital."
10528,"(10528) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Omar Abi Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was desirable To satisfy the needs of the Ahl al-Bayt with it, meaning zakat."
10529,"(10529) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: He will be given from it whatever is between him. And between two hundred."
10530,"(10530) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Habib, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: He will give him of it what is between him. And between two hundred."
10531,"(10531) Omar bin Zur’a told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Amer, who said: Give from the zakat what is not permissible for anyone. You give him zakat."
10532,"(10532) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, and Abd By God, they said: It is not permissible to give charity to someone who has fifty dirhams, or an amount of gold."
10533,"(10533) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever asks his guardian for what will benefit him will receive scratches, or Weary on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: O Messenger of God, and what is his singing? He said: Fifty dirhams, or an amount of gold. (Tirmidhi 651, Abu Dawud 1623)"
10534,"(10534) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He should not be given zakat to someone who has fifty dirhams. He shall not be given more than fifty dirhams of it."
10535,"(10535) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Hassan used to say: He should not give of it to anyone who has fifty dirhams, nor He will be given more than fifty of it, unless he owes a debt in which case his debt is paid off, and he is given after fifty"
10536,"(10536) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I heard Hammad saying: Whoever does not have money amounts to On it is zakat, it was given from zakat."
10537,"(10537) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: I asked Ibrahim about the companions of Passions? He said: They only asked about the needy."
10538,"(10538) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he delivered Muadh to Yemen, and ordered him to take alms from wheat and barley. So he took the offerings of clothing made of wheat and barley."
10539,"(10539) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Omar used to take gifts of charity from papers and other things."
10540,"(10540) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Muadh said: Bring me Khamis, or I am taking something from you."
10541,"(10541) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus; That Muadh used to accept offers in charity."
10542,"(10542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Antarah; That Ali used to take offers in the Jizah from the people of the needles, from the people of the liquefied, and from the people of the ropes. Ropes"
10543,"(10543) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to love zakat on everything from it; Paper is from paper, gold is from gold, cows are from cows, and sheep are from sheep."
10544,"(10544) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated the offer of charity."
10545,"(10545) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Najih, claiming that Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz wrote about the date charity: The barni is to be taken from the barni, and the color is from the colour, and the color is not to be taken from Barney."
10546,"(10546) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: He gave it to you in one of the eight categories that God Almighty has named and rewarded."
10547,"(10547) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Hudhayfy said: If you put it in any As many types as you like, I will reward you if you do not find anything else."
10548,"(10548) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, or someone else, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Hudhaifa, He said: If he puts it in one category, that is acceptable."
10549,"(10549) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Omar used to take what was offered in charity and give it in one type of what God Almighty has named."
10550,"(10550) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: It suffices for you. To place charity in one of the categories that God Almighty has named."
10551,"(10551) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: There is no harm in You place it in one category of what God Almighty said."
10552,"(10552) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked him: Give alms in one category. The eight? He said: Yes."
10553,"(10553) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in placing it in one category. The eight"
10554,"(10554) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: There is no harm in putting them in one category. From what God Almighty has named."
10555,"(10555) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Spend it in the categories. Al-Hasan said: Which of them did you put your parts in?"
10556,"(10556) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: I heard him say: If I put the zakat in These two types: The poor and the needy, I would have thought that this would be enough for me."
10557,"(10557) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, that Abu Amr bin Hamas He told him that his father Hamas used to sell human beings and jabs, and that Omar said to him: O Hamas, pay the zakat on your money, so he said: By God, I have no money. I only sell human beings and animals. So he said: Evaluate them and pay their zakat."
10558,"(10558) Zaid bin Harun and Abdou told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, On the authority of Abu Amr bin Hamas, that his father Hamas used to sell human beings and jabs, and that Omar said to him: Then he mentioned something like him, Or something like that."
10559,"(10559) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who bought something and zakat was permissible on it? He said: He will pay zakat on it at its value on the day it was released."
10560,"(10560) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no zakat on gifts, Except for an item in trade, for that is zakat."
10561,"(10561) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said regarding the belongings: It is prepared, then it is paid. Zakat"
10562,"(10562) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; About a man who buys goods and stays there for years, paying zakat on them? He said: No."
10563,"(10563) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Everything with which I want to do business is in it. Zakat, even if it is milk or clay. He said: The arbitrator thought so."
10564,"(10564) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Uqba, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: When Abu Bakr used to give to people The Giving man asked: Do you have any money? If he says: Yes, he will pay zakat on his wealth from his gift, otherwise his gift will be handed over to him."
10565,"(10565) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It was He gives us gifts through the Messengers, so we purify them."
10566,"(10566) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, he said: He was Ibn Masoud. He pays zakat on their gifts out of every thousand and twenty-five."
10567,"(10567) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman Ibn Abd al-Qari, and he was in charge of the Bayt al-Mal during the time of Omar with Abd Allah Ibn al-Arqam. When donations were made, Omar would collect money. Commerce, according to the immediate and later ones, then zakat is taken from those who are present and those who are absent."
10568,"(10568) Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Uqba, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: Abu Bakr used to give a man a gift. He asked him, then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Waki`."
10569,"(10569) Abd al-Rahim and Waki` told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq, that Omar ibn al-Khattab was He gives them gifts but does not purify them."
10570,"(10570) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I saw the princes when they were given gifts. He paid zakat"
10571,"(10571) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He used to purify gifts and rewards."
10572,"(10572) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; He used to give gifts and purify them."
10573,"(10573) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hanafiyyah; In the words of God Almighty: {And give His due on the day of their harvest} They said: It was abrogated by the tenth and the half-tenth."
10574,"(10574) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was abrogated by the ten And half a tenth."
10575,"(10575) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, who said: They used to give something other than charity."
10576,"(10576) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hayyan Al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, in the Almighty’s saying: {And give His due on the day of its harvest} He said: Zakat."
10577,"(10577) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Zakat."
10578,"(10578) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, and Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; {And they gave their due on the day of their harvest} He said: They used to give to anyone who disobeyed them anything other than charity."
10579,"(10579) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ata’; In his saying: {And give him his due on the day of your harvest} He said: Whoever is present with you on that day, you will give him the same amount, but not zakat."
10580,"(10580) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; In the words of God Almighty: {And give your due on the day of your harvest} He said: When you reap it and the poor attend you, you will pour out for them some of it, and when you mash it You poured out some of it for them, and when you stacked it up you rolled out some of it for them, and when you purified it and took in its entirety, you gathered it up for them. And when you know how much you pay zakat on it, and when you take the trunks of palm trees, you give them some of the fruits and dates, And when you take its measure, you will pay them some of it, and when you know its measure, you will pay zakat on it.
 (10580 AD) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in the Almighty’s saying: {And give His due on the day of your harvest} He said: His zakat on the Day of Kaila."
10581,"(10581) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, who said: This is Medina and Mecca, its ten copies. And half a tenth, I said: from whom? He said: On the authority of the jurists. What God Almighty says means: {And give His due on the day of harvest}"
10582,"(10582) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: {And they came His due on the day of his harvest} They said: He will give you a burden."
10583,"(10583) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Like al-Daghath."
10584,"(10584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was abrogated by zakat."
10585,"(10585) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Zakat abolishes every act of charity in the Qur’an."
10586,"(10586) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Atiyya, he said: It was abrogated by the tenth and the half-tenth."
10587,"(10587) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; In the Almighty’s saying: {And give his due on the day of its harvest} He said: Zakat on the day of its harvest."
10588,"(10588) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {And give His due on the Day of Reaping} its abrogation is the tenth and the half-tenth."
10589,"(10589) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will come out in its place."
10590,"(10590) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of his companions, who said: If he pays the zakat on his wealth and it is lost, let him pay it again. Other"
10591,"(10591) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who sends his charity and it is destroyed before it reaches its people. He said: In the same position as a man who was sent to He owed him a debt, but the money did not reach him until he died."
10592,"(10592) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: It is not sufficient."
10593,"(10593) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man, if he pays zakat on his wealth and it is lost, it is sufficient for him."
10594,"(10594) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who paid the zakat on his wealth and it was lost. He said: It will not suffice until he places it in its proper place."
10595,"(10595) Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: It will come out in its place."
10596,"(10596) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar informed me, on the authority of Tawus, saying: If The two people are working with their money, so their money will not be combined in charity."
10597,"(10597) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I told Ata’ about what Tawoos said, and he said: I only see it as the truth."
10598,"(10598) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he used to say: If a man has twenty sheep, And another man had twenty sheep, and their shepherd was one, and they set sail together and return together. He said: Zakat is due on them."
10599,"(10599) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, Salama’s client, who said: Salama used to show the truthfulness of Iblis. He refused to buy it."
10600,"(10600) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn Ata, on the authority of Muslim ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: No. You buy the purity of your property."
10601,"(10601) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu Al-Zubair told me that he heard Jabir say: If The charity came, so give him your charity, and do not buy it. He said: They say, “Buy it,” but I say: No, it is for God."
10602,"(10602) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I asked him: Does a man buy his charity? He said: He will not buy it from the believer until he brings it out, and he will not buy it when he brings it out until it is mixed with sheep. A lot"
10603,"(10603) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Indeed, those who passed away disliked buying their alms. He said: And if you do it after it has been collected from you, there is no problem with it."
10604,"(10604) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar was mounted on a horse for the sake of God. He saw it, or some of his clothes being sold in the market, so he wanted to buy it and asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Leave her until she meets you on the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 1239. Ahmad 1/25)"
10605,"(10605) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam; That a man was riding a horse for the sake of God, and he saw a horse or foal being sold that was attributed to his horse, so he forbade it. (Ibn Majah 2393. Ahmad 1/164)"
10606,"(10606) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; Abu Usama carried a dowry for him in the name of God, and after that he saw a ripe foal being sold. He said: So I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I knew his knowledge, but he forbade me from it. (Tabarani 4668)"
10607,"(10607) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: If charity turns into something other than that, you give charity. There is no harm in him buying it."
10608,"(10608) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar carried a horse for the sake of God, and saw it being sold in the market, so he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to buy it. He said: No, leave her until she meets you on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 2775. Muslim 4)"
10609,"(10609) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zaid bin Harithah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, similar to the hadith of Asama."
10610,"(10610) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; He was asked about a man who benefits from his charity? He said: His reward will be reduced in proportion to the amount of it he has achieved."
10611,"(10611) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jadham bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, On the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the purchase of charity until You are arrested (Ibn Majah 2196. Darqutni 44)"
10612,"(10612) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus; He was asked: Should he buy his charity before it is given? His thoughts"
10613,"(10613) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Charity is not bought until it is marked and given to it."
10614,"(10614) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: Charity cannot be bought until it is marked."
10615,"(10615) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Because they hated for a man to buy something with his own charity, until it was transferred from the charity."
10616,"(10616) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of Jabir; He heard him forbidding the sale of charity before it is given."
10617,"(10617) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of more than one person; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the sale of charity until it is collected and branded."
10618,"(10618) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, that Omar asked a man about land of his own. Did they sell it? So he said to him: Save your money, and dig for it under your wife’s bed. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, is there no treasure? He said: It is not a treasure unless its zakat is paid."
10619,"(10619) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab He said: Whoever pays his zakat is not a treasure."
10620,"(10620) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Any property that has been paid zakat is not With a treasure"
10621,"(10621) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Ibn Umar, similarly."
10622,"(10622) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He has not paid his zakat. It is not a treasure."
10623,"(10623) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: There is no treasured wealth that has to be paid its zakat. Even if it is under the earth, and if zakat is not paid on it, then it is a treasure, even if it is on the face of the earth."
10624,"(10624) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man was found to have ten thousand after He died and was buried. He said: They said: This is a treasure. He did not pay its zakat. Ibn Umar said: Perhaps he did. About her from others."
10625,"(10625) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to see in their wealth any right other than zakat."
10626,"(10626) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {In their wealth there is a known right}, he said: apart from zakat."
10627,"(10627) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Aamir, who said: There is a right in money other than zakat."
10628,"(10628) Muadh narrated to us, saying: Hatim bin Abi Saghira Abu Yunus narrated to us, saying: Riyah bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Qaz’a, he said: I said to Ibn Omar: I have money, so what do you command me to whom I should pay its zakat to? He said: Give it to the ruler of the people, meaning the princes, but there is no right other than that, O Qaz’a."
10629,"(10629) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, he said: Muzahim bin Zufar told me, he said: I was sitting with Ata’. Then a Bedouin came to him and asked him: I have camels, do I have any right to them after giving alms? He said: Yes."
10630,"(10630) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever pays zakat Whatever his wealth, there is no blame on him if he does not give it in charity."
10631,"(10631) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is a right in money other than zakat."
10632,"(10632) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s wife came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. She said: In the stones of my brother’s sons are a crown of mine. Would it be sufficient for me if I put my zakat on my ornaments on them? He said: Yes. (Bukhari 1466. Muslim 45)"
10633,"(10633) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in putting your zakat on Your relatives, unless they are among your dependents."
10634,"(10634) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Indeed, he is most deserving of the one I repelled. To Him are my zakat, my orphan and my relatives."
10635,"(10635) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; That his wife asked him about the children of a brother who had orphans in her family, would she give them zakat? He said: Yes."
10636,"(10636) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abi Hafsiya, who said: I asked Sa`id ibn Jubayr about Maternal aunt, will she be given zakat? Saeed said: Unless a door is closed on you."
10637,"(10637) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and on the authority of Hisham, or someone else, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They both made a concession regarding kinship."
10638,"(10638) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: I said to Ata’: Is it rewarded for a man to give birth? Zakat on his relatives? He said: Yes, if they are not with his family."
10639,"(10639) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If you have poor relatives, they are more deserving. With your zakat from others."
10640,"(10640) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: I asked Abraham about a sister, is she given zakat? He said: Yes."
10641,"(10641) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; What about a man giving his zakat to his relatives? He said: Yes, as long as they are not with his family."
10642,"(10642) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus, who said: A man asked him, and he said: Do you have some poor people? He said: Take it out from you and your family."
10643,"(10643) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Umm al-Raihih bint Sali’, on the authority of her paternal uncle Salman. Ibn Aamir al-Dhabi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Charity towards someone other than a relative is charity, and against a relative two; Sincerity and connection (Tirmidhi 658, Nasa’i 2363)"
10644,"(10644) Abu Bakr said: And I heard someone mentioning, on the authority of Sufyan, that he said: It should not be given to someone who is forced to do so. Your expense"
10645,"(10645) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Tha’labah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not accept the kinship of a woman in need."
10646,"(10446) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; About a man giving his zakat to a poor person, then it turns out that he is rich? He said: That is sufficient."
10647,"(10647) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who gives from his zakat to a rich man, and he does not know? He said: It is not sufficient."
10648,"(10648) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Alani, who said: I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bailili saying: Sword jewelry is one of the treasures."
10649,"(10649) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, who said: I said to Makhul: O Abu Abdullah, I have A sword that contains fifty and a hundred dirhams. Do I have to pay zakat on it? He said: Add to it whatever gold and silver you have, and you must pay zakat on it."
10650,"(10650) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’, Hammad, and Ibrahim about the silver cup and the sword. If I collect it and there are two hundred dirhams in it, should I pay zakat on it? They said: No."
10651,"(10651) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Malik bin Abdullah Al-Kala’i, who said: I heard Malik bin Mughal say: Sword jewelry is one of the treasures."
10652,"(10652) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If you are in debt, do not pay zakat."
10653,"(10653) Abd al-Rahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; In the case of a man who is in debt for one year and two years, should he pay zakat on him? He said: No."
10654,"(10654) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man pays zakat to another man His money, he looked at what the people had and isolated him."
10655,"(10655) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Fudayl, who said: Do not sacrifice what people have over you."
10656,"(10656) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Zakat has a specified limit, so if that is fulfilled, it is sufficient. It is the property of the one who is present and the one who is absent, so he will pay on his behalf except what he owed."
10657,"(10657) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: Put away whatever debt you owe, then pay off what you owe. He stayed"
10658,"(10658) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Zayd, who said: I heard Uthman say: This is the month Pay your zakat. Whoever is in debt, let him pay it off, and pay zakat on the rest of your wealth."
10659,"(10659) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who is in debt and has money in hand. Is this a joke? He said: Yes, he has to pay zakat. Don’t you see that he is guarantor? And Rabiaa asked? He said: Like what Hammad said."
10660,"(10660) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abdullah bin Rawahih to Yemen to plant palm trees for them. He said: I asked Al-Shaabi: Should he do it? He said: No. (Tabarani 2136)"
10661,"(10661) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When God sends Al-Kharis, may God bless him and grant him peace, he will command him not to cut down bare palm trees. (Abdul Razzaq 721)"
10662,"(10662) Abu Dawud and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Masoud says: Saul bin Abi Hatham came to our gathering, and it happened that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If You have drawn up, then take and leave a third, and if you do not find a third, then take a quarter. (Tirmidhi 643 and Abu Dawud 1601)"
10663,"(10663) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar; Omar used to send Abu Khaythama to search for palm trees, and he said: When you come to the Ahl al-Bayt in their area, do not search. They are responsible for what they eat."
10664,"(10664) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he heard him say: Ibn Rawahih chose it, meaning Khaybar, forty thousand wasqs, and he claimed that when the Jews gave them the option, they took Dates, and they owe twenty thousand wasqs."
10665,"(10645) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Make it easy for the people in the amount of money, for in money there is the common and the low.
 He said: The palm tree that a man inherits is within the man’s garden. And the homosexual is a man who recommends homosexuality to the poor. (Abu Ubaid 1453)"
10666,"(10646) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Attab ibn Asid to prune grapes just as palm trees are pruned, so that the harvest should be harvested. The zakat is paid on raisins, just as the zakat on palm trees is paid on dates. This is the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding palm trees. And grapes (Tirmidhi 644, Abu Dawud 1599)"
10667,"(10667) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Karim and Amr ibn Dinar said to me: He should be shortened. Palm trees and grapes, but the grain is not lost."
10668,"(10668) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: When will the palm trees be harvested? He said: When he feeds you."
10669,"(10669) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Juraij said: Abdullah bin so-and-so told us; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that Khaybar be cut off when its dates were good. He said: And Ibn Shihab said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the khaybar be ground when the first dates are cooked. (Abdul Razzaq 7216)"
10670,"(10670) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: The plow of a man whose debt is greater than his wealth. So it was harvested. Will he pay his due on the day of his harvest? He said: We do not see that a man has a debt greater than his wealth than his charity in livestock or in any asset, unless he pays it back. His truth is the day of his harvest, the day he reaps it."
10671,"(10671) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubair said to me: I heard a peacock saying: He is not on him. He spoke the truth"
10672,"(10672) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil; He was responsible for the tithes, so he used to make people swear to them, so Abu Wael passed by him and said: Why do you make people swear about their money? Throw them in Hell? He said: If I had not asked them to swear, they would not have given anything. He said: It is better for them not to give you than for you to swear to them."
10673,"(10673) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: It was stolen on the chain, so he was the one who passed by it. He gave him something beforehand and said: Do you have something to which we have a right? If he says yes, otherwise he says to him: Go."
10674,"(10674) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, he said: I passed by Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman with a ship, and what He left me until he made me swear what was in it."
10675,"(10675) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: Omar sent me to pay the tithes, and ordered me not to search for anyone."
10676,"(10676) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The tenth was only to guide the wayfarer, and whoever He brought him something before him."
10677,"(10677) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Harb bin Ubad Allah, on the authority of his maternal father’s grandfather, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Muslims are not obligated to tithe, but the tithe is due to the Jews and Christians. (Abu Dawud 3041)"
10678,"(10678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Harb bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his maternal uncle, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, like the hadith of Abu Al-Ahwas. (Abu Dawud 3042. Ahmad 3/474)"
10679,"(10679) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, he said: Whoever heard Amr bin Al-Muhajir narrated to me. Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: O Arabs, thank God. Who set the tithes for you. (Ahmad 1/1901 Abu Ali 964)"
10680,"(10680) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Two kisses are not appropriate on earth, and no penalty is imposed on a Muslim. (Abu Dawud 3048. Ahmad 1/223)"
10681,"(10681) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: Omar sent me to Al-Sawad, He forbade me from paying tithing to a Muslim or a non-Muslim who pays the tax."
10682,"(10682) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas; The Thaqif delegation came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they stipulated that they should not be gathered together, nor be given ten, nor It is obligatory, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is yours not to be gathered together, not to be given a tithe, and not to be appointed over you. Other than you (Abu Dawud 3020, Ahmad 4/218)"
10683,"(10683) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: Omar sent me to the Christians. My son was defeated, and he ordered me to take half a tenth of their wealth."
10684,"(10684) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Saffah bin Matar, on the authority of Dawud bin Kurdous, on the authority of Omar bin The speech; He made peace with the Christians of his people, so that the zakat should be doubled on them twice, and on those who did not convert to Christianity in a small way, and that They should not be forced to adopt the religion of others. David said: They are not under any obligation. They have become Christians."
10685,"(10685) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: I was with my grandfather and he passed by. He met a Christian with a horse worth twenty thousand, and he said to him: If you wish, you can give two thousand, and if you wish, you can take the horse and we will give it to you. Its value is eighteen thousand."
10686,"(10686) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz; That Omar sent Uthman bin Hanif, and he assigned to the people of the religion their wealth over which they disputed in every twenty years. A dirham, a dirham, and he wrote about that to Omar ibn al-Khattab, agreeing to it and allowing it, and he said to Omar: How much do you order us to take from the merchants? People of war? He said: How much will they take from you if you come to their country? They said: The tenth. He said: Likewise, so take from them."
10687,"(10687) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah; Omar ibn al-Khattab appointed his father and another man to collect the alms of non-Muslims over which they disputed to Medina, so it was He ordered them to take half of the tithe of wheat, to make it easier for them, to carry it to Medina, and of the cotton. These are the ten grains."
10688,"(10688) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is taken from the people of the people of the religion of every Twenty dirhams is one dirham, and from the people of war, from every ten dirhams, one dirham, and from the people of non-Muslims if they trade in wine, From every ten dirhams, one dirham."
10689,"(10689) Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Raziq, the client of Banu Fazara. Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to him: Take from the non-Muslim merchants who pass by you some of their wealth that they show. And they make money from the trade, from every twenty dinars, and whatever decreases from it, they will calculate what is decreased, until it reaches ten, So if three dinars decrease, leave them and do not take anything from them, and write for them a release for something similar within the year, including take from them"
10690,"(10690) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about the Christian penalty of a dog. And overcome? He said: We have learned that half a tenth of their livestock is being taken from them."
10691,"(10691) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: Omar appointed me to Al-Masir, so I was giving tithes to those who came before and after, then a man came out to him and informed him, so he wrote to me: Not to give tithes except to one woman. Meaning, in the Sunnah."
10692,"(10692) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghalib ibn al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Christian came to Omar. He said: Your worker paid tithes twice a year, so he said: Who are you? He said: I am the Christian sheikh. Omar said: I am the Hanafi sheikh. So he wrote to his worker: Not to give tithes during the year except to one woman."
10693,"(10693) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Hudayr, who said: I am the first to He tithed in Islam."
10694,(10694) What they said about the poor and needy: Who are they?
10695,"(10695) Abu Asama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, he said: A man told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; He was asked about the poor and needy? He said: The poor: those who are chaste, and the needy: those who ask."
10696,"(10695) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, who said: I heard Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim say: {But Alms are for the poor and needy. He said: the poor: those who emigrated, and the needy: those who did not emigrate."
10697,"(10696) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Maqil narrated to us, saying: I asked Al-Zuhri about the saying of God Almighty: {Only Alms for the poor}? He said: The poor: those who are in their homes and do not ask, and the needy: those who go out and ask of Me."
10698,"(10697) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a bin Salih, on the authority of Yahnas, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Bedouins are truthful. Breakfast"
10699,"(10698) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Bedouins are not required to pay zakat al-fitr."
10700,"(10699) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Talha, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah bin Saeed bin Al-Aas said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq used to take ground mushrooms from the Bedouins."
10701,"(10700) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They are given milk."
10702,"(10701) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: The Bedouins give alms of breaking the fast, a saa’ of milk."
10703,"(10702) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who frees a Christian slave, he said: I have committed him under the protection of his master."
10704,"(10703) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is not obligated to pay the jizya."
10705,"(10704) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who frees a Christian slave, he said: He must pay the Jizya."
10706,"(10705) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sinan; Omar bin Abdulaziz took the jizya from a Christian who was freed by a Muslim."
10707,"(10706) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, who said: I asked Omar bin Abdul Aziz about the land of the tax, Does she have to pay zakat? He said: The tax is on the land, and the zakat is on the grain."
10708,"(10707) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The tax is on the land, and the tithe is on the grain."
10709,"(10708) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: There is no zakat on dates if they are A tenth is taken from it, even if it is in the amount of one hundred thousand."
10710,"(10709) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan and Sufyan used to say: Ali."
10711,"(10710) Ibrahim bin Al-Mughirah told us about the circumcision of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Sukari, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi He said: A tax and a tithe cannot be combined on one land."
10712,"(10711) Abu Tamila Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Munib, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A tax is not collected. And a tenth of money."
10713,"(10712) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hanifa used to say: A man’s tax and zakat are not combined."
10714,"(10713) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim bin Muhammad; In his saying: {And those in whose wealth there is a known right}, he said: Zakat."
10715,"(10714) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And those in whose wealth there is a known right}. He said: the obligatory zakat."
10716,"(10715) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When it came out, Give some of their gifts in charity."
10717,"(10716) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik took the money of a man from the people of slavery. It was said to him: Abu Aisha gave him twenty thousand, so he threw it into the treasury. When Omar bin Abdul Aziz took over, his son came to him. So they reported their injustice to him, so he wrote to Maimun: Give them their money, and take the zakat of this year, had it not been It was a lost property from which we took zakat over the past years."
10718,"(10717) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Maimun; That a man had money due to some injustices, and it fell into the treasury, so when Omar bin Abdul Aziz took over, it was brought to him. So Omar wrote: Give it to him, and take from him the zakat of what he has passed. Then he followed them after writing: Give him his wealth. Then take the zakat from it for that year, for it was rich wealth."
10719,"(10718) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He must pay zakat that year."
10720,"(10719) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah: {And they withhold help}. He said: This is what people dispute among themselves. The axe, the pot, the bucket, and the like."
10721,"(10720) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ubaidin, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: This is what people consult among themselves."
10722,"(10721) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali; {And they withhold the aid} He said: the obligatory zakat. Ibn Abbas said: Bare the belongings."
10723,"(10722) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali, who said: Al-Ma’un al-Zakat."
10724,"(10723) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It is the money that He is not given his rights."
10725,"(10724) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabi’i, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It is money. The one who does not fulfill his rights."
10726,"(10725) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan (H) and Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ayyad, on the authority of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they said: Al-Ma’un means the protection of the axe, the pot, and the bucket."
10727,"(10726) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Subh, on the authority of Umm Sharahil, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: Al-Minah."
10728,"(10727) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Al-Ma’un prevents the axe. And destiny and bucket."
10729,"(10728) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Her family has not come yet."
10730,"(10729) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Qadr and Al-Rahhi. Some of them said: the axe."
10731,"(10730) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Zakat."
10732,"(10731) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Destiny and bucket."
10733,"(10732) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah, similar to him."
10734,"(10733) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama ibn Kulayl, on the authority of Abu al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: This is zakat."
10735,"(10734) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, similar to the hadith of Ibn Masoud."
10736,"(10735) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar; That Abu Al-Ubaidin asked Abdullah about the utensils? He said: It is the axe, the pot, and the bucket."
10737,"(10736) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Omar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Al-Ma’un Zakat"
10738,"(10737) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Al-Ma’un is money in the language of Quraysh."
10739,"(10738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bassam, who said: I asked Ikrimah about Al-Ma’un? He said: The axe, the pot, and the bucket."
10740,"(10739) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Heirlooms"
10741,"(10740) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The obligatory zakat is what is provided for."
10742,"(10741) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: We lent the Sa’ of Medina. We found him exceeding a measure more than Al-Hajjajji."
10743,"(10742) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, who said: Al-Hajjajji is a Saa’ of Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab"
10744,"(10743) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Qafiz Al-Hajjaji is the saa’."
10745,"(10744) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abraham did not give a fatwa regarding expiation for a right or wrong oath. Purchasing, or feeding sixty poor people, and regarding what he said about it: a tenth and a half tenth, he said: he used to give a fatwa with a reward. Al-Hajjaji said: It is the saa’."
10746,"(10745) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: I heard Hassan saying: A lifetime’s saa’ is eight pounds. A partner said: More than seven pounds and less than eight."
10747,"(10746) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Siwar, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father, he said: He was sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us, seeking, so he took alms from our rich and divided it among our poor, and I was a boy. An orphan, so He gave me a few drops of her blood. (Tirmidhi 649. Darqutni 7)"
10748,"(10747) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar was asked about what is taken from Bedouin alms, how to do with them? Then Omar said: By God, I will give them charity, until a hundred camels or a hundred camels go to one of them."
10749,"(10748) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He took half of the Bedouins’ alms, and gave half of it back to our poor."
10750,"(10749) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Salim bin Abdullah was dividing Omar’s charity, and the man came to him. A possessor has given it to him, and he says: Give it to me, and he gives it to him and does not ask of it."
10751,"(10750) Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Sahl, he said: I saw Othman on the way to Mecca, and alms were given to him, and the man who was separated from him was given them."
10752,"(10751) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Sharik Ibn Namli, who said: Ali sent me seeking truthfulness. He said: So my brother accompanied me, so I gave in charity. He said: So I carried my brother on a camel, so I said: If Ali rewards him, otherwise it is from my wealth, so when I came to him and told him the story of my brother, and he said: You have a share in it."
10753,"(10752) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Aslam; Omar sent camels from Al-Sadaqah to Al-Hama, and when I wanted to leave, he said: Show them to me, so I showed them to him. I set my groomsmen on one of her she-camels, and he said: You have no mother. I went to a she-camel that was being carried to life by a Muslim family. Does she have to wear it? Was Ibn Labun not a urinator or a camel?"
10754,"(10753) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwarith, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: There is no zakat on property except for property you own."
10755,"(10754) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of his mother, who said I went to Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, he said, and he was in charge of the treasury in the authority of Omar and in the authority of Uthman, and he was dividing it in charity. In Medina, when he saw you, he said: He did not bring you, Umm Ziyad. She said: I said to him: When the people came to him, he said: Have you been freed yet? I said: No, so he sent for his house and brought a piece of hail, so he ordered it for me, but he did not order for me any of the charity because I was Owned"
10756,"(10755) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not feed these Sudanese people from your sacrifices, for it is only This is the wealth of the people of Mecca."
10757,"(10756) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Salim, that he disliked giving alms to the Bedouin slaves. (Tabarani 3233)"
10758,"(10757) Abd al-Rahman and Waki` told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abbas bin Abd al-Rahman al-Madani, who said two characteristics did not The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give them both to one of his family. He used to give food to the poor in his hand and put Purification for oneself."
10759,"(10758) Wakī’, on the authority of Abu al-Manāl, who said: I saw Ali bin Hussein wearing a camel and wearing a quilt, and I saw him He gives food to the poor with His hand."
10760,"(10759) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked him about the man. Does he lend loans to the people of the earth or is he in debt? Should he pay zakat? He said: Yes."
10761,"(10760) Waki`, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: There is no zakat on Mudarib because he does not know what Made"
10762,"(10761) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far (and the debtors), he said: Those who spend in other than Corruption, (and the wayfarer) one who crosses the land to the other."
10763,"(10762) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, three of the debtors said: A man who had a flow. With his money, and a man was afflicted with a fire, so he lost his money, and a man who had children but had no money, so he will be judged and will be spent on. His family"
10764,"(10763) Waki’, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said to the debtor: The imam should pay off his debt."
10765,"(10764) Al-Zubayri Abu Ahmad, he said: Maqil told us, he said: I asked Al-Zubayri about the debtors: the people of religion said, And the wayfarer, even if he is rich."
10766,"(10765) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Rayhan bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to a straight man. (Tirmidhi 652, Abu Dawud 1631)"
10767,"(10766) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to someone who is bitter."
10768,"(10767) Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Habashi ibn Junada, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: The issue is not permissible for a rich person, nor for a person who is bitter."
10769,"(10768) Abdul Rahim and Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Adiy bin Al-Khiyar, he said: Two men told me that they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him for truthfulness. He said, so he raised He saw it and corrected it, and said: Indeed, you will be flogged, and he said: If you wish, I will give it to you, and no rich person will have any share in it, nor Strong and acquired.
(Abu Dawud 1630, Ahmad 5/362)"
10770,"(10769) Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: It is not desirable to be truthful. He is rich, and he has no right mind."
10771,"(10770) Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, brother of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The issue will remain with one of you until he meets By God, there is not a trace of flesh on His face. (Bukhari 1474, Muslim 103)"
10772,"(10771) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said, “If only the person in question knew.” What is in it is what he asked. (Tabarani 12616)"
10773,"(10772) Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Whoever asks the people without a scholar will come on the Day of Resurrection. There are scratches or scratches on his face."
10774,"(10773) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Umm al-Darda’ said to Abu al-Darda’: If I need to eat charity after you? He said: No, work and eat. She said: If you are too weak to work, he said: Pick the ears of ears, and do not eat alms."
10775,"(10774) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Uqba, or So-and-so bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every matter is distress on the face of a man on the Day of Resurrection, except that He asks a ruler, or about an urgent matter. (Tirmidhi 681, Abu Dawud 1636)"
10776,"(10775) Ibn Fudail, on the authority of Ammarah ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever asks people for their wealth in abundance is only asking for a hot coal, so let him take some of it, or To increase it. (Muslim 1050, Ahmad 2/231)"
10777,"(10776) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Habashi Al-Saluli, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Whoever asks people to enrich himself with his wealth, there will be scratches on his face and scorn from Hell that will eat him up one day. Resurrection, and that is during the Farewell Pilgrimage."
10778,"(10777) Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: Omar said: Whoever asks people to enrich his wealth with it, it is only him. A source of Hell, so whoever wishes, let him reduce it, and whoever wishes, let him increase it."
10779,"(10778) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: Because one of you takes a crop of wood and goes to the mountain, collects firewood from it and sells it, and eats and gives in charity. It is better than asking people. (Bukhari 1480, Muslim 107)"
10780,"(10779) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubair, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Because one of you takes a lamb and goes and brings a bundle of firewood on his back and sells it, and God will suffice. For his sake, it is better for him than for him to ask people for something, to give it to him, or to deny him something. (Bukhari 3075. Ahmad 1/167)"
10781,"(10780) Muhammad bin Bishr and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Whoever asks excessively will come on the Day of Resurrection with blemishes on his face."
10782,"(10781) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: A questioner came and asked So he gave him something, and it was said to him: Will you give it to him while he is well off? He said: Indeed, he is a questioner, and the questioner has a right, and he will be granted hope on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, it was a mercy in his hand."
10783,"(10782) Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, conveying the message to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted: Whoever asks if he has a uqiyya, or has just enough of it, then he asks the people urgently. (Abu Dawud 1424, Malik 11)"
10784,"(10783) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person except for three people: in the path of God, or a wayfarer, or a man who has A neighbor, so you gave him alms and gave him gifts. (Abu Dawud 1634, Bayhaqi 23)"
10785,"(10784) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is not permissible to give charity except to five people: a man who bought it with his own money, or a man who worked on it, or a wayfarer, or a… For the sake of God, or a man who had a neighbor who gave alms to him and he gave him gifts. (Malik 29)"
10786,"(10785) Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Habashi ibn Junada al-Saluli, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: A Bedouin came to him and asked him, and he said: The question is not permissible except in cases of extreme poverty or a heavy debt."
10787,"(10786) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that a questioner asked Ibn Umar, Al-Hasan, Al-Hussein, and Abdullah bin Ja’far, and they said: If you ask about a terrible debt, or extreme poverty, or, he said, a painful loss, then charity is permissible for you."
10788,"(10787) Al-Fadl bin Dukin, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Harun bin Ri’ab, on the authority of Kinanah bin Na’im, on the authority of Qabisa bin Al-Mukhariq Al-Lalali said: I carried a burden and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask him about it. He said: Stay, O Qubaysah, until you bring us charity and we will command it for you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him. And he greeted him: O Qubaysah, the issue is not permissible except for one of three people: a man who carries a burden for him, and the matter is permissible for him until It afflicts it, then it catches you. And a man was afflicted by a plague that ravaged his wealth, so the matter was resolved for him until he became afflicted with a family. of subsistence, then he is caught, and a man who has been afflicted with him has survived until three people of the Hajj from his people say, “She has afflicted So-and-so is poor, and the matter is resolved for him until he earns a living, then he is caught, O Qubaysah, and no one else. Among the issues is something unlawful that was eaten by its owner. (Muslim 1091, Abu Dawud 1637)"
10789,"(10788) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, about a man who traveled while he was rich, and what he had with him ran out on his journey. And he needed? He said: He is given some of the charity while he is on a journey because he is a wayfarer."
10790,"(10789) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is self-sufficient, God will enrich him, and whoever is chaste, God will pardon him, and the Most High Hand is better than The lower hand. (Bukhari 1427, Muslim 95)"
10791,"(10790) Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id and Urwah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hizam, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand. (Bukhari 2750, Tirmidhi 2463)"
10792,"(10791) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Hamza narrating on the authority of Hilal bin Hisn, he said: I stayed in a house Abu Sa`id joined me and him in the gathering, and he told me that one day in the morning his stomach was hurting from hunger. He said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I realized what he said and he said: Whoever is chaste, God will pardon him, and whoever God seeks to be self-sufficient, and whoever asks us, we will either do it for him, or we will console him. And whoever seeks help, or seek pardon from us. It is better for him than to ask us. He said: I returned and did not ask him anything. (Nasa’i 2369. Ahmad 3/44)"
10793,"(10792) Ali bin Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not need people, even if only with a toothpicks. (Bazzar 913)"
10794,"(10793) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, in the same way, And he did not raise it."
10795,"(10794) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were talking about the Supreme This is the chaste one."
10796,"(10795) Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Asim Ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is so long as it preserves wealth, and start with those you depend on."
10797,"(10797) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi, on the authority of Aswad bin Hilal On the authority of Tha’labah bin Zadam, he said: A group of Tha’labah went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was delivering a sermon. He says: The hand of the giver is the upper one, and the hand of the beggar is the lower one. And start with those you depend on: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and your lowest. So we approached you (Tayalisi 1257, Musnad 634)"
10798,"(10798) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Aqna’. Al-Bailili, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais, who said: I was sitting in a gathering in Medina, when a man arrived, whose throat you could not see, but they fled. From there, he reached the circle that I was in, so he remained steadfast and they fled, so I said: Who are you? He said: Abu Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So I said: Why do people flee from you? He said: Indeed, he forbade them from treasures. He said: I said: Our gifts have reached and increased, so you fear for us from them. He said: But Today, no, but it is about to be the cost of your religion, so call on them and them."
10799,"(10799) Ibn Idris, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: We passed by Abu Dharr about Al-Rabdhi, and we asked him about His house, he said: I was in the Levant and I read this verse (And those who hoard up gold and silver, but do not spend In the way of God, give them good tidings of a painful punishment.) He said: Mu'awiyah is only among the People of the Book, so we said: Indeed, he is among us. And in them."
10800,"(10800) Ibn Fudail, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: And by Him there is no god. Other than Him, God will not punish a man who hoards a dirham for a dirham, or a dinar for a dinar, but He expands his skin until Every dirham and dinar is placed separately."
10801,"(10801) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: I heard Abdullah say regarding the words of God Almighty: {They will encircle that which they were stingy with on the Day of Resurrection} He said: {They will encircle} a snake with two raisins in its mouth. What is your money that you were stingy with?"
10802,"(10802) Ali bin Ubaid, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is no owner of camels, cows, or sheep who does not pay his due but sits for them for a day. Standing in a turbid place, a female with a hoof will trample it with her hoof, and a female with a horn will gore it with her horns, but it will not be in it on that day. They said: O Messenger of God, and what is the right to it? He said: He loosed her stallion, lent her her bucket, gave her a goat, milked her on the water, and carried her for the sake of God. (Muslim 27 Ahmad 3/321)"
10803,"(10803) Zaid bin Hubab, he said: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to me, he said: Imran bin Abi Unais narrated to me, on the authority of Malik Ibn Aws Ibn Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or my beloved say: In He who collects a dinar, or a dirham, or a lump of earth, or silver, does not give it back to a debtor, nor spend it on it. The way of God will be ironed with it on the Day of Resurrection. (Daraqutni 27. Bayhaqi 147)"
10804,"(10804) Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, in the words of God Almighty: {They will encircle what they were stingy with on the Day of Resurrection} He said: an encirclement. From fire"
10805,"(10805) Khalaf bin Khalifa, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Masruq, in the Almighty’s saying: (They will encompass what they were miserly with.) On the Day of Resurrection) He said: He is a man to whom God will bestow wealth, but He will withhold from him the right that is in him, and He will be made a serpent. So he encircles it and says: What is mine and what is yours? Then the snake says: I am your owner."
10806,"(10806) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Harira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Some of the al-Sadaqa dates were brought to him. Al-Hasan ibn Ali ate some dates and licked them in his mouth. He said to him: Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Good luck, good news. It is not permissible for us to give charity. (Bukhari 1491, Muslim 161)"
10807,"(10807) Waki’ and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Ammar, on the authority of a sheikh called Rabi’ bin Shayban, He said: I said to Al-Hasan bin Ali, may God be pleased with them, “What do you mention, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what do you understand from him?” He said She took one of the dates of zakat and ate it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible for us to give zakat.
(Ahmad 1/2001 Tabarani 2741)"
10808,"(10808) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, found A date, and he said: Were it not from charity, I would have eaten it. (Bukhari 2055, Muslim 166)"
10809,"(10809) Abdou told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: It is not permissible to give charity to the Banu Hashim, nor For their followers"
10810,"(10810) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abi Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, sent a man from Banu Makhzum to the charity, and he said to Abu Rafi’, “Do you accompany me as much as you can do with her?” He said: “No.” Until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, and he said to him: Charity is not permissible for us, and the people’s friends are from themselves. (Tirmidhi 657, Abu Dawud 1647)"
10811,"(10811) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, that Khalid bin Saeed was sent to Aisha was given cows from charity, but she returned them and said, “We are the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it is not permissible for us to give charity.”"
10812,"(10812) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Qurayh al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, he said I gathered firewood, sold it, brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and placed it in his hands. He said: What is this? I said he was telling the truth, so he told his companions to eat, but he did not eat. (Ahmad 5/438, Hakim 108)"
10813,"(10813) And on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I came to Umm Kulthum bin Ali with some truthfulness. She returned it and said: A servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who is called Mihran, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: We are the family of Muhammad, and it is not permissible for us to give charity and the servant of the people among them. (Ahmad 3/448 and Abd al-Razzaq 6942)"
10814,"(10814) Al-Hasan bin Musa, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of his father, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the House of Sadaqa. He said: Then Al-Hasan bin Ali came So he took a date, took it from him, took it out, and said: It is not permissible for us to give it in charity. (Ahmad 4/348, Darami 1643)"
10815,"(10815) Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: Husayn ibn Uqba and I set out for Zaid bin Arqam, and Zaid and Husayn said to him, “Aren’t his wives from the people of his household?” He said: His wives are from his family, but his family are those who were forbidden to give charity after him. Husayn said to him: And who are they? He said: They are the family of Abbas, the family of Ali, the family of Jafar, and the family of Aqeel. So he said to him: They are strong over these. Charity is forbidden. He said: Yes. (Muslim 36 Ahmad 4/367)"
10816,"(10816) Kathir ibn Hisham, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, said: Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, saying, “I was informed that two men from The children of Abdul Muttalib came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him about charity, and he said: No, but if you see me with me Something of the five came to me."
10817,"(10817) Waki`, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not permissible. They gave them alms, so He made for them one-fifth. (Nasa’i 4449)"
10818,"(10818) Al-Fadl bin Dukain, he said: Ma’rif bin Wasil narrated to us, he said: Hafsa bint Talaq narrated to me, she said: My grandfather narrated to me. Rashid bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible for us to give charity. (Bukhari 1131. Ahmad 3/489)"
10819,"(10819) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The one who works to do truthfulness with the truth is like one who fights in the path of God. Until he returns to his home. (Tirmidhi 645. Abu Dawud 2929)"
10820,"(10820) Abu Osama, on the authority of Buraid bin Abdullah bin Abi Burda, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, the trustworthy treasurer is the one who gives what he is commanded to do in full, providing himself with peace of mind at the time. He gives it to the one who was ordered to do it by one of the charitable people. (Bukhari 1438 and Abu Dawud 1681)"
10821,"(10821) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim Al-Makki, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab sent a man from He is very trustworthy and trustworthy. He saw him after that day and said: Shall I not see you and you will receive the reward of a fighter for the sake of God?"
10822,"(10822) Abu Asama and Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Zakat is given to Him, and He places it in its proper place, and it has the reward of its owner."
10823,"(10823) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, that Amr ibn Al-Khattab appointed the people of Every garib is a qafiz and a dirham."
10824,"(10824) Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Omar appointed eight days on the palm tree. drama"
10825,"(10825) Ali bin Mushir, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Awn Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Al-Thaqafi, said: Omar bin Al-Khattab is upon the people of Sawad, upon every barren land that reaches the level of water, abundant and abundant with a dirham and a large amount of food, and upon the orchards. For each gerib of land ten dirhams, and ten dirhams of food, and for the vineyards, ten dirhams for each gerib of land. He paid ten dirhams of food, and five dirhams were imposed on each land grater, and five dirhams of food were given to him. The palm trees were a thing, and He made them a part of the land, and the rich man’s heads were forty-eight dirhams, and the middle ones’ Twenty-four dirhams, and the poor man owes twelve dirhams."
10826,"(10826) Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Omar put black on the black and mentioned a similar hadith Ibn Mushar (Abu Ubaid 174)"
10827,"(10827) Abu Usama, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Umar sent Uthman ibn Hanif as governor The land, so Othman placed ten dirhams on the grape vine, eight dirhams on the palm tree, and eight dirhams on the barley grape. Two dirhams, and he imposed on each head twenty-four dirhams for the year, and he granted women and boys a leave of absence."
10828,"(10828) Waki’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Omar, that he sent Uthman ibn Hanif to control Al-Sawad, and he put On every land-grave, inhabited and overwhelming, the waterer will receive a dirham and a qafiz, meaning wheat and barley, and on every land-grave of generosity. Ten dirhams, and each wet jarib is charged five."
10829,"(10829) Waki`, on the authority of Ali ibn Salih, on the authority of Aban ibn Taghlib, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Umar, that he placed palm trees on The two rakalahs are a dirham, and the Persian one is a dirham.
 Waki` bitterly said: On the authority of Aban, on the authority of Abraham."
10830,"(10830) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: Concerning a man, if he is given some of his zakat al-fitr, he says: If he has the best of the two, he will give it to him."
10831,"(10831) Hafs, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, Al-Sha’bi, and Ibn Sirin, they said: Sadaqat al-Fitr is given to the rich. And the poor."
10832,"(10832) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’, he said: He takes and gives."
10833,"(10833) Malik bin Ismail, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Do not give zakat al-fitr To whom it is permissible to give charity, he said: Al-Zuhri said: He fulfills the rights of God and takes it."
10834,"(10834) Affan, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of his leaders, he said: He gives you."
10835,"(10835) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: We have not been informed that anyone of his governors These are the nations who were in Medina, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman. They used to give charity, but They are sent to it every year in abundance and barrenness, because they took a tradition from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
10836,"(10836) Muhammad bin Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me, on the authority of Tawoos, that he said when The two alms are combined, so the first is not taken as a reward."
10837,"(10837) Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Hassan bin Hassan, on the authority of his mother Fatima, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: There is no double in charity."
10838,"(10838) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of three people, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in charity from some of the Banu Hashim. On some."
10839,"(10839) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said that charity is only for the poor. And immigrants."
10840,"(10840) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr: that Uthman used to give zakat al-fitr, on the authority of The rope"
10841,"(10841) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: They used to give zakat al-fitr until they were given, About the rope."
10842,"(10842) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the authenticator takes one tooth upon another, he will return to them two sheep. Or twenty dirhams, and if he takes a tooth under a tooth, they return to him two sheep, or twenty dirhams."
10843,"(10843) Muhammad bin Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Khallad told me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that he said to him, If you do not find the tooth below it, you take the tooth above it and return to the owner of the livestock two sheep, or twenty dirhams."
10844,"(10844) Muhammad bin Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Al Ansari, that Omar wrote to some Do not take from a man whose camel you do not find the tooth on, except that tooth."
10845,"(10845) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, regarding a man whose camels were obligatory for a religious duty that was not with him, he said: He said: They seek mutual favor between themselves."
10846,"(10846) Al-Fadl bin Dukain, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said that He took a tooth less than a tooth and returned two sheep, or ten dirhams."
10847,"(10847) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Mustarid narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Qalaab narrating to Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz, he said: Abu Bakr sent the believers and ordered them to sell the Jad`a for forty and the Haqqi for thirty, and Ibn Labun for ten, and Bint Makhad for ten, so they set off and sold what they sold for Abu Bakr’s value, then they returned until, when The next year he sent them, and they said: If we wish to increase, we will increase. He said: Increase in every age ten, so when the year was He sent them next, and they said: If we wished to increase, we could increase a little. So when Omar took office, he sent his workers at the value of Abu Bakr. Until the next year, the workers said: If we wanted to increase, we would increase, so he said: Increase every ten years until If the next year was a mission for them with the other value, they said: If we wish to increase, we will increase. He said: No, not even if Othman takes charge. He was sent with the value of a lifetime until the next year. They said: If we had wished for more, we would have increased. He said: Increase for every age. Ten times, even if it was the next year. They said: If we had wanted to increase, we would have increased. He said: No. Then when Mu’awiyah took over, he sent his money. Othman the last year, and when the next year came they said: If we wish to increase, we will increase. He said: Increase every ten years, until then The following year they said: If we wanted to increase, we would increase. He said: Take the obligations by the teeth. Then they elevated them and announced them. Then they created them for sale, but they were not able to diminish, and you were not able to increase, so they increased. Abdullah said: Then I saw Omar bin Abdul Al-Aziz, as if he did not see anything wrong with that, so he said to Abu Qalabab: So how was the sheep’s charity? He said: Charity used to be taken and distributed among the poor people of the desert until Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan ordered it to be given. So it was divided into fifths, and he allocated a fifth of it to the needy, and that has not ceased to this day."
10848,"(10848) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Buffaloes are in the same position as cows."
10849,"(10849) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about a man who neglected to pay his zakat until he went What is his money? He said: It is a debt he owes until he pays it off."
10850,"(10850) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: When there is wheat and barley on the earth, each one Of it, there are less than five awasaqs, so if they are combined, there are five awasaqs of it, or more, then there is truthfulness in both of them, because It is all of crops, so if it contains wheat and raisins and it does not reach five wasaqs, then there is nothing in it until it reaches the size of each. It is a type of five awasaq, and if it reaches it, then one tenth is required."
10851,"(10851) Abdul Salam, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, he said: In every ten cows there is a sheep, and in every Twenty sheep, and for every thirty you sell."
10852,"(10852) Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, who said: I used the alms of Akka, and I met some people who He ratified the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the cows. I asked them and they disagreed over me. Some of them said, “Make it like The camels spoke the truth, and among them were those who said, “There are thirty tabee’s,” and among them were those who said, “There are forty cows.” An elderly cow."
10853,"(10853) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about a man who bought from his zakat a sum of money. So he freed her, and Al-Nasmah died and left behind an inheritance. He said, “He will give her zakat purposes.”"
10854,"(10854) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Imran Al-Qattan, he said: Al-Hasan was asked: Does a woman have to pay zakat on her wealth? According to her husband’s appearance, he said, “If he is rich, then he must pay zakat on her.”"
10855,"(10855) Ishaq Al-Azraq, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he said: A woman must pay zakat on her marriage if it is On her husband if he is well-off, and if he is poor, then she does not owe anything."
10856,"(10856) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: If it were for a man, nineteen A dinar that has no other value, and the exchange rate is twelve, or thirteen in which there is zakat? He said: Yes, if it had been spent for two hundred dirhams, then it was only paper, and not gold."
10857,"(10857) Abdul Salam, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Among the Sunnah regarding charity is to take a headband with every camel. And with every camel, two headbands and a qaraan."
10858,"(10858) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abu Bakr said: If they withhold from me a punishment from They gave to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because of your struggle against him."
10859,"(10859) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Harith, in the words of God Almighty: (And perform prayer and pay zakat) He said: He meant it. The truth of nature"
10860,"(10860) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: The zakat of breaking the fast is a prescribed saa’."
10861,"(10861) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, and Ibn Sirin, who said: Sadaqat al-Fitr is obligatory."
10862,"(10862) Abu Usama, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Bukhari 1504, Abu Dawud 1607)"
10863,"(10863) Yazid bin Harun and Saul bin Yusuf, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the Messenger of God said: It is an obligation May the peace and blessings of God be upon him."
10864,"(10864) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The only ones whose hearts are bound are upon a covenant. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when Abu Bakr took charge, it ceased."
10865,"(10865) Waki`, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, his author said: Today is the author."
10866,"(10866) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad was asked, about those who reconcile their hearts, so he narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They enter Islam."
10867,"(10867) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi, he said: Maqil told us, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri: about those whose hearts are broken, he said: He is someone who converts to Islam, whether a Jew or a Christian. I said: Even if he is rich. He said: Even if he is rich."
10868,"(10868) Affan, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Hamid told us, on the authority of Hayyan al-Salami, he said: I told Ibn Umar They will come to me as believers of Ibn al-Zubayr, and they will take my charity, and they will come to believe in our help, and they will take it? He said: Which one of them you have given is sufficient for you?"
10869,"(10869) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He took away a dinar from every dreamer."
10870,"(10870) Hatim bin Ismail, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said while he was sitting between the grave and the pulpit: I know what to do with the Magians, who are not People of the Book. So Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Learn the way of the People of the Book.” (Malik 42. Abdul Razzaq 10025)"
10871,"(10871) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Shuaib narrated to me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: A man said, O Messenger of God, he was not on the road other than dead, or in the inhabited town. He said, “In it, and in the five pillars.” (Ahmad 2/180, Hamidi 597)"
10872,"(10872) Abd al-Wahhab, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: In the five pillars."
10873,"(10873) Waki’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the same."
10874,"(10874) Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid and Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In the five pillars. (Ahmad 2/493)"
10875,"(10875) Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar story."
10876,"(10876) Abu Usama, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that an Arab boy found a camel containing ten thousand, so he came to it. Omar took from it five thousand and gave him eight thousand."
10877,"(10877) Waki’, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that a man found in Kharbiyah one thousand and five hundred So he came to Ali and said: Give five of it, and three-fifths of it is yours, and we will prepare the remaining fifth for you."
10878,"(10878) Mu`ammar, on the authority of Muammar al-Dhabi, who said, “While my people were with sabours, they were softening, or they were stirring up the earth, when they struck A treasure, and Muhammad bin Jabir al-Rasibi was in possession of it, so he wrote about it to Adiyy, so Adiyy wrote to Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz, So Omar wrote, “Take the fifth from him, and write for them the disavowal,” and they left the rest of it for them. So he gave them water and took the fifth from them."
10879,"(10879) Hushaym, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of the one who witnessed al-Qadisiyyah, who said: While a man was bathing, the water found the dirt on him. Milk of gold, so Saad bin Abi Waqqas came and told him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
10880,"(10880) Ibn Idris, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Qays Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: A man came to Abdullah, and he said: I found two hundred dirhams, and Abdullah said: I do not see Muslims whose wealth has reached this, I see it. Ordinary capital, so pay a fifth of it to the treasury, and you get what remains."
10881,"(10881) Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The rikaz is the ordinary treasure, and in it is the fifth."
10882,"(10882) Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If the treasure is found in the enemy’s land, then one-fifth is in it, and if It is found in the Arab land and it is subject to zakat."
10883,"(10883) Ghandar, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, that a man asked Aisha and said: I found a treasure and gave it to the sultan, and she said, “You have a cat in your mouth,” or a word similar to it. Doubt is on my part."
10884,"(10884) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: In the five pillars. (Bukhari 1499, Muslim 1335)"
10885,"(10885) Khalid bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Kathir bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: In the five pillars. (Ibn Majah 2674. Tabarani 6)"
10886,"(10886) Al-Fadl bin Dukain, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling regarding the five pillars. (Ahmed 314)"
10887,"(10887) Al-Fadl, he said: Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He was asked about a man who found a buried grave. He said: Five of them"
10888,"(10888) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Bakr, he said: My father told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque while some people were hanging in the mosque, and when there was someone hanging in it, there were walls in it, and with him A limp, or a stick. He stabbed it and said: Who brought this? They said: So-and-so. He said: Miserable are people who hold back their alms, then they are thrown away with the naked clothes, and they do not eat them. Well-being is the reward of every lightning. And he returned to the Levant (Abu Dawud 1404). Ahmad 6/28."
10889,"(10889) Abu Usama, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Hafsiya, who said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, who said: Some people used to give in charity the worst of their fruits until they were revealed {And do not complete the evil of it; Close your eyes to it}"
10890,"(10890) Ibn Aliyah, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he asked his servants about the Almighty’s saying: (And (You will spend the evil from it, but you will not take it.) That is only in zakat, and counterfeit dirhams are more beloved to me than dates."
10891,"(10891) Wakī’, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan {And do not complete the evil of it that you spend} He said: The man used to give in charity. With his wealth"
10892,"(10892) Ubayd Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Al-Bara’, in the Almighty’s saying: {And do not perform tayammum The Wicked} He said: It was revealed about us when we were the owners of palm trees, and the man used to come from his palm trees as few as they were and as many. He said: Then a man would bring a Qanwi, and another man would bring a Qanun, and he would hang it in the mosque. He said: And the people of The Saffites had no food, so when one of them came, the Qunu would come and hit him with a stick, and he would drop some of the dates and whole grains and eat. And there were some people who did not desire good, and one of them would go to the Quno, and there would be filthiness in it, and there would be porcupine in it, and he would come. With the qanū, it has been broken, so it is suspended. He said: Then God Almighty revealed: {And do not complete the evil thereof, ye shall spend, and you will not take it unless That you close your eyes to it.} He said: If one of you were given something like what he was given, he would not take it except with his eyes closed and wide. He said: After that, the man would bring whatever good he had. (Tirmidhi 2987 and Ibn Majah 1822)"
10893,"(10893) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man whose fruit was allocated for him, and there was an advantage over what was allocated for him. He said: Whatever is in excess, he will have it, and whatever it is short of, he will make up for it."
10894,"(10894) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: We asked Abraham twice for zakat."
10895,"(10895) Hushaym, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I brought him zakat and he accepted it. He said: And they told me that Some of the people of Badr accepted it."
10896,"(10896) Abd al-Salam, on the authority of Amr ibn Musawar, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he did not think there was anything wrong with a man hastening to give alms that broke the fast. A day or two before breaking the fast."
10897,"(10897) Abu Usama, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when someone sat down he would arrest He broke the fast two days before breaking the fast, or the day he gave it to her, a day or two before breaking the fast, and he does not see that. It's unfortunate"
10898,"(10898) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: Whoever asks God and He gives him seventy rewards. (Bayhaqi 3540)"
10899,"(10899) Waki’ told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he hated to be asked. In the face of God, or by the Qur’an for any matter of this world."
10900,"(10900) Hammad ibn Mas’ad, on the authority of Zayd, Salama’s client, who said: Salama was such that no one would ask him for the sake of God. Nothing but He gave it to him and rejected it and said, “It is a burden.”"
10901,"(10901) Ali bin Mushir, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever asks of God, He will be given to him. (Abu Dawud 5068. Tabarani 13540)"
10902,"(10902) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, he said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us, and he does not tithe wine. Muslim"
10903,"(10903) Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He takes a tenth of the wine and doubles it."
10904,"(10904) Waki`, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafali, that the workers of Omar wrote To him regarding the pigs and wine, they took them as a tribute, so Omar wrote that their masters had appointed them as their guardians."
10905,"Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us:
(10905) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, he said : I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was feeling sick. He said, I touched him and said: O Messenger of God, you are truly unwell. Severe, so he said: Yes, I am as weak as two men among you are. He said: I said: Because you have two rewards? He said: Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, there is not a single person on the earth who is safe and afflicted with harm, and there is nothing else except that which God has removed from it. His sins are as a tree sheds its leaves. (Bukhari 5647. Muslim 1991)"
10906,"(10906) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The believer will not be struck by a thorn or anything above it, unless God raises him by it a degree or lowers it from him. Bad (Muslim 1991, Tirmidhi 965)"
10907,"(10907) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Saleh Al-Ash'ari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he returned sick and with him was Abu He saw that he was suffering from an illness, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rejoice. Indeed, God says: This is a fire I will control.” upon My believing servant in this world so that he may have his share of the Fire in the Hereafter. (Tirmidhi 2088 and Ahmad 2/440)"
10908,"(10908) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Muhaisin, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makramah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: When these verses were revealed: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it}, it was difficult for the Muslims and disgraced some of them, and they complained about it to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Approach and repay, and everything that a Muslim is afflicted with is an expiation, even the calamity. Its stings and thorns prick it. (Muslim 1993, Tirmidhi 3038)"
10909,"(10909) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhammara, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of the Muslims is afflicted with calamity in his body except by God’s command. memorizers, and he said: Write down for My servant what he used to do, and it is correct as long as he is bound by his bonds. (Ahmad 2/1591 Darami 2770)"
10910,"(10910) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of the Awwam, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Moses said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever falls ill, or travels, God will record for him whatever he did in good health. resident (Bukhari 2996 and Abu Dawud 3084)"
10911,"(10911) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, on the authority of Ata ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa`id and Abu Hurairah said that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: What befalls a believer from And no illness, no adversity, no sickness, no sadness, even worry, except that God pardons some of his sins from him. (Bukhari 5642, Muslim 1992)"
10912,"(10912) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Bashar bin Abi Saif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Iyadh ibn Ghataif, he said: We entered upon Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah to go back to him, when he faced him from the wall next to him. And his wife was sitting at his head. I said: How did Abu Ubaidah spend the night? She said: He spent the night with a reward, so he turned to face us. He said: I did not spend the night with any reward, and whoever God tests with affliction in his body, then he will be humiliated."
10913,"(10913) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim told us that he heard it from Bashar bin Abi Saif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, reported the same to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 1951 Bukhari 93)"
10914,"(10914) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Muawiyah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: There is nothing that befalls a believer in his body that harms him unless he disbelieves in it. From his bad deeds. (Tabarani 842)"
10915,"(10915) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: I mentioned a fever with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man cursed her, so he said to him: No. It purifies sins just as fire purifies impurities from iron. (Ibn Majah 3469)"
10916,"(10916) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The trial will never cease to befall the believer, male and female, until he meets God and all that is upon him. A sin (Hakim 346)"
10917,"(10917) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, who informed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: When a servant becomes ill, God says to the honorable scribes, “Write for My servant the like of what he used to do.” Until I arrest him, or recover him."
10918,"(10918) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Sa’id bin Mawhib, who said: I set out with Salman to A friend of his returned from Canada, and he said: God afflicts a believer with calamity, then He recovers him, and he is expiation for his misdeeds, and he will be reproached for what remains, but the ungodly one will be afflicted by God with calamity, then he will recover, and he will be Like a camel, its people have killed it, but it does not know why they killed it, then they sent it, but it does not know why they sent it."
10919,"(10919) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Fudail bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, he said: He said Salman: If a servant falls ill, the king says, O Lord, you have afflicted your servant with such and such. He said: Then he says, “As long as he is in my bonds, write down a proverb for him.” His work that he used to do."
10920,"(10920) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, saying: I heard Urwah bin Ruwaym mentioning on the authority of Al-Qasim On the authority of Muadh, he said: When God afflicts a servant with sickness, He says to the companion of the left, “Get up,” and He says to the companion of the right, “Write down for My servant what He was working."
10921,"(10921) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Wa’il narrating on the authority of Aisha, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or anything above it except that God will exalt him with it. degree and removed his sins. (Bukhari 5640, Muslim 1991)"
10922,"(10922) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Abi Tamimah, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: There is no pain. It afflicts me more beloved to me than fever, for it enters every joint of the son of Adam, and God will give every joint a fair share. Of the reward."
10923,"(10923) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim, who said: One day Abu Al-Darda’ saw a man and was astonished by his flogging. Abu Al-Darda’ said: Have you ever had a bath? Have you ever had a fracture? The man said: No. Abu Al-Darda’ said: How miserable is this man? He dies because of his sin."
10924,"(10924) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Umayla, on the authority of Ammar, He said: There were Bedouins with him and they mentioned pain, so he said: Ammar, have you ever complained? He said: No. So he said: Ammar, you are not one of us, or You are not one of us. There is no servant who is tested except that his sins are removed from him just as a tree sheds its leaves. Indeed, the disbeliever will be tested. His likeness is like that of a camel that was let loose but did not turn when it was let loose."
10925,"(10925) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Al-Aliyah entered upon Al-Nadr bin Anas to return him, and he said: We were We have been talking for fifty years, that there is no servant who falls ill but that he rises from his illness as on the day his mother gave birth to him, and we were talking Fifty years ago, no servant fell ill without God saying to His scribes: Write down for My servant what he used to do in Your health"
10926,"(10926) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, he said: He said: Abdullah, the reward is not written for pain, but for it sins are expiated."
10927,"(10927) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Darda’ said what I am pleased with a night filled with red camels."
10928,"(10928) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: If a man falls ill after doing a good deed, whatever happened to him will happen to him. He works on his health."
10929,"(10929) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If a man becomes ill, all One day he was working."
10930,"(10930) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, who said: If a servant becomes ill The best of what he did in his health was recorded for him."
10931,"(10931) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein said: If the body does not become ill, it is worse. There is no good in a body that does not bring good."
10932,"(10932) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: No man is pricked by thorns. Above that, God removed his sins from him."
10933,"(10933) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: I said, O Messenger of God, what? The people are the most severely afflicted. He said: The prophets. Then the best of the people. And the servant will continue to be afflicted until he meets God and what is upon him. A sin (Tirmidhi 2398 and Ibn Hibban 2900)"
10934,"(10934) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha ibn Umairah, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Yahud The people of calamity on the Day of Resurrection, that their bodies in this world were being cut with scalds."
10935,"(10935) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Everything is written from the sick person, even His groaning in his illness."
10936,"(10936) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Rabi’ah told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: When God afflicts a Muslim with affliction in his body, he says to the angel: Write For him is the good deed that he used to do. If he heals him, he washes him and purifies him, and if he takes him away, he forgives him and has mercy on him.
(Ahmad 148. Bukhari 501)"
10937,"(10937) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Bashir, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, On the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever visits a sick person does not He will remain in the depths of Paradise until he returns."
10938,"(10938) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Thawban, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Muslim 1989. Tirmidhi 968)"
10939,"(10939) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Omar bin al-Hakam bin Thawban, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever visits a sick person will continue to enter the womb until he sits down, and lo! He sat and immersed himself in it. (Bukhari 522, Ahmed 304)"
10940,"(10940) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Abu Musa went to Al-Hasan bin Ali about his return, and he was complaining. He said to him: Ali: Did you come back, or did you gloat? He said: No, but he is returning. Then Ali said to him: When you came returning, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Who has come? His Muslim brother, he returns to walking in the myths of Paradise until he sits, and when he sits, mercy will overwhelm him, and if his morning is, he prays Seventy thousand angels will pray over him until the evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels will pray over him until the morning.
(Abu Dawud 3092. Tirmidhi 969)"
10941,"(10941) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of some of the family of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that he came to Ali and said to him: What brings you? Did you come back? He said: I do not know of any of you complaining. He said: Yes, Al-Hasan bin Ali. Then Ali said: Whoever visits a sick person during the day, pray. Seventy thousand angels will be upon him until the evening, and whoever returns at night, seventy thousand angels will pray upon him until the morning."
10942,"(10942) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, he said: It was narrated If a man visits a sick person, he immerses himself deeply in the womb, but when he sits, he immerses himself in it completely."
10943,"(10943) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Bashar bin Abi Saif told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever visits a sick person, or removes an affliction from his path, I will reward him tenfold. (Ahmad 1/1951 Abu Ali 875)"
10944,"(10944) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Musa Al-Janni narrated to us, saying: I heard Saeed bin Abi Burda, saying: My father told me that Abu Musa set off to return to Al-Hussein bin Ali, and Ali said to him: Are you returning, or are you a visitor? He said: No, but a visitor. He said: He does not prevent me, even if it is in your mind, what is in your mind is that I should tell you; When a pilgrim left his house, he would come back sick. He would go deeply into mercy, but when he came to the sick person, he would sit down. Mercy has overflowed upon him, and he returns from the sick. When he returns, seventy thousand angels will accompany him, seeking forgiveness for him during the day. All in all, even if it is night, he will remain in that abode until morning, and there is Kharif in Paradise."
10945,"(10945) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’ath’i Al-Muharbi, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to attend to the sick and to attend funerals.
(Bukhari 1239. Tirmidhi 1760)"
10946,"(10946) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu Isa al-Aswari, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Visit the sick person and follow the funeral procession, so that the afterlife will remind you.
(Abdullah bin Hamid 1001, Abu Ali 1114)"
10947,"(10947) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He greeted the Muslim: the Muslim has the right to visit him if he falls ill and attend his funeral. (Tirmidhi 2736. Ahmad 1/89)"
10948,"(10948) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, how did you wake up in the morning? He said: Better than a man who did not fast in the morning and is no longer sick. (Bukhari 133)"
10949,"(10949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama bin Wardan, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his companions: Who among you witnessed a funeral? Omar said, “I.” He said: Who among you visited a sick person? Omar said, “I am.” He said, “Who gave alms?” Omar said, “I am.” He said: Who among you is fasting in the morning? Omar said, “I am.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is obligatory, it is obligatory. (Ahmad 3/118, Tabarani 11)"
10950,"(10950) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It is the right of a Muslim upon another Muslim to witness the funeral and attend to the sick. (Bukhari 519, Ahmed 357)"
10951,"(10951) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When they were asked about a sick person, they loved to say: Saleh, then they will mention his pain afterward."
10952,"(10952) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: When you attend the sick person or the dead, say good, for the angels believe in what you say. (Muslim 6. Tirmidhi 977)"
10953,"(10953) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Ansar used to recite Qur’an at the dead. Surah Al-Baqarah."
10954,"(10954) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Umm al-Hasan, who said: I was with Umm I greeted her and looked at her head. Then a person came and said: So-and-so is dying. So she said to him: Go. When he is dying, say peace to him. On the Messengers, and praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds."
10955,"(10955) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I was informed that Muhammad ibn Sirin attended some of his family while he was in Death, so he started saying: Say peace, say peace."
10956,"(10956) Uqba bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If you enter upon a sick person and comfort him during his term, then that does not avert anything and is It freshens the soul of the sick. (Tirmidhi 2087 and Ibn Majah 1438)"
10957,"(10957) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Umayyah al-Azdi, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, that it was Surah Al-Ra'd is recited at the time of the dead."
10958,"(10958) Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, but not By Al-Nadi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maqil bin Yassar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Recite it when... Your dead, meaning Jesus.
(Abu Dawud 3112 and Ibn Hibban 3002)"
10959,"(10959) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When they attended a dying man, they would take out the menstrual period."
10960,"(10960) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, a woman came to him and said: I am being treated. He is sick, so I stand up for him while I am menstruating, and he said: Yes, so when he comes, avoid his head."
10961,"(10961) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in a menstruating woman being present. The dead"
10962,"(10962) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Teach your dead, “There is no god but God.” (Muslim 2. Ibn Majah 1444)"
10963,"(10963) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Omar said: Bring your dead and remember them, there is no god Except Allah, for they will see it and it will be said to them."
10964,"(10964) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Instruct your dead. There is no god but Allah."
10965,"(10965) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said, when his feet became heavy, he said, “Sit with me.” He reminds me that there is no god but Allah."
10966,"(10966) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Alqamiya and Al-Aswad advised me to teach me no. There is no god but Allah."
10967,"(10967) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’ or someone else, who said: Omar said: Teach your dead that there is no god but God. Except Allah"
10968,"(10968) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Was it desirable for the dead to instruct? He said: Yes, it is good. I would like that."
10969,"(10969) Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man who fell ill and became heavy. He said: They did not like him to be alone, and they would pursue him when people got up. Others would come and teach him not to do so. There is no god but Allah."
10970,"(10970) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, he said: Ammar bin Ghazi al-Ansari narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Teach your dead not to There is no god but Allah. (Abu Dawud 3108, Tirmidhi 976)"
10971,"(10971) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Al-Aswad advised a man, and he said: If you are able That this be the last thing I say: There is no god but Allah, so do so, and do not place any reward in my grave."
10972,"(10972) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, who said: Al-Nadr bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the people of Al-Medina, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, that a man complained to you, and he said: Convince him, there is no god but Allah, for it is the last His words enter Paradise. (Abu Dawud 3107, Ahmed 233)"
10973,"(10973) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, who said: “Whoever says there is no god but Allah upon his death” He entered Paradise."
10974,"(10974) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Al-Walid Ibn Muslim narrated to me, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Uthman, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but God will enter Paradise (Muslim 43 Ahmad 69)"
10975,"(10975) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sharik told me, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: Teach your dead, “There is no god but Allah,” for it will not be the last speech of a Muslim except that God will make it sacred to him in the Fire."
10976,"(10976) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Yahya bin Abi Rashid told me. Al-Basri said: Omar said to his son when death approached him: If death approaches, then distort me."
10977,"(10977) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like for him to face him. The dead person before him when he is present."
10978,"(10978) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was desirable to meet the dead. The kiss if it is in death."
10979,"(10979) Omar bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said: It was desirable for the dead to face his face. When we turn to the Qiblah? He said: Yes."
10980,"(10980) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If you wish, visit the dead person, and if you wish, then do not Your guidance"
10981,"(10981) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that He hated it and said: Isn’t the dead person a Muslim?"
10982,"(10982) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, he said: When it was On the night Hudhayfy died, Abu Masoud came in and said: Step aside, your night has been long. So he leaned him on his chest and he woke up. He said: What time is this? They said: magic. Hudhayf said: O God, I seek refuge in You from the morning to the Fire and the evening therein. Then We made him lie down and he died."
10983,"(10983) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, he said: Zar’i bin Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that he testified Saeed bin Al-Musayyab was ill, and Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman was with him. Saeed fainted, so Abu Salma ordered him to His bed was turned towards the Kaaba, so he woke up and said: Have you moved my bed? They said: Yes, so he looked at Abu Salamah and said: I see what you did, so he said: Yes, I ordered them, so he said, Sa`id ordered that they be brought back. His bed"
10984,"(10984) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When you close your eyes for the dead, say: In the name of God and upon the death of the Messenger. May God bless him and grant him peace."
10985,"(10985) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Qubaysa bin Dhu’ayb, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, closed his eyes to Abu Salamah. (Abdul Razzaq 6050)"
10986,"(10986) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Rashid al-Basri, who said: Omar said, when the death of his son approached him, “If I die, then cover me with your eyes.”"
10987,"(10987) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, closed his eyes A man's eye"
10988,"(10988) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, or someone else, who said: Omar said, “Tell your dead that there is no god but God.” Except Allah, and close their eyes when they die."
10989,"(10989) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the dead person is washed, the Between him and the sky is a curtain."
10990,"(10990) Azhar Al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, that Muhammad used to cover the dead with his utmost effort."
10991,"(10991) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: There is no harm for a man to perform ghusl in public space. He disliked that the dead be washed in this way."
10992,"(10992) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, who said: Ali washed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in a shirt. (Abu Dawud 3133. Malik 222)"
10993,"(10993) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Abu Qalaab told me: Cover him as much as you can."
10994,"(10994) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, washed his body. And peace be upon Ali, and upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, his shirt, and Ali’s hands are rags with which he washes him, so he enters He puts his hand under the shirt and washes it with the shirt on him. (Bayhaqi 388)"
10995,"(10995) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: When they wanted to wash the Prophet, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He was wearing a shirt and they wanted to take it off, so they heard a call from the house: Do not take off the shirt. (Ibn Saad 275)"
10996,"(10996) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Do not strip me."
10997,"(10997) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It was desirable for the sword to be placed On the belly of the dead."
10998,"(10998) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Hafsiya, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them about washing his daughter: Start with her right place and the places where ablution is performed. (Bukhari 1256, Muslim 42)"
10999,"(10999) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Hafsa told me, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: The Messenger of God entered upon us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while we were washing his daughter, and he said: Start with her right and the places where ablution is performed. (Abu Dawud 3137. Ahmed 85)"
11000,"(11000) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that when he was asked about washing the dead, he said: It begins with On his right and the places of ablution on his right."
11001,"(11001) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He begins with the dead, and his ablution is performed. For prayer, then he begins with his right."
11002,"(11002) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It begins with the dead, and he performs ablution for prayer."
11003,"(11003) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His ablution is performed for prayer except His legs"
11004,"(11004) Muadh and Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: His ablution is performed. To pray"
11005,"(11005) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Al-Mughairi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said The dead person is performed ablution as for prayer, except that he does not rinse his mouth or blow his nose."
11006,"(11006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The dead person is performed ablution just as a living person is performed."
11007,"(11007) Ghandar, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan and Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab that they said: Ablution is performed in the dead. His ablution for prayer."
11008,"(11008) Yahya bin Ali Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: Mujahid came to us while we were washing a dead person. He said: Perform ablution as you perform prayer."
11009,"(11009) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon us. May God bless him and grant him peace while we were washing his daughter. He said: We washed her three times, or five times, or more than that, if you see us. That is with water and Sidr, and in the afterlife put camphor, or something of camphor. So when you have finished, then announce to Me. And when We have finished, We will announce to you. So he threw his loins to us and said: Let us know it. (Bukhari 1259, Muslim 646)"
11010,"(11010) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: When Zainab, the son of the Messenger of God, died May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: We washed it once, three times, or five times, and put camphor in the last part, or something of camphor. So when We have washed it, let us know about it. So when We have washed it, let us know about it, so He gave us its loins and said: Make it feel to me. (Muslim 40) Ahmed 85)"
11011,"(11011) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan, who said: He is washed. The dead person was given three washings, or three galls, passed with water and lotus tree, passed with water from ulcers, and passed through with water and camphor."
11012,"(11012) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The dead are washed three times and a sider is placed in the washing. Al-Wastaiya."
11013,"(11013) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The dead person should be washed three times with Sidr. And water."
11014,"(11014) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The dead person is performed ablution for prayer except his feet, then water is poured over his head and his stomach is wiped, and if anything comes out, then he is left, until You said it dried, or almost, he washed the second and third time, and his clothes were rolled up three times."
11015,"(11015) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one who washes the dead sits for a period of time between each two washings. He is resting."
11016,"(11016) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The dead person should not be rinsed out, nor should he be rinsed, but a rag should be taken. Clean, so he wipes his mouth and nostrils with it."
11017,"(11017) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Farqad al-Sabkhi, on the authority of Abu Tamim al-Jamimi, that Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, saying: Wash your hands with Sidr and basil water."
11018,"(11018) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said: Abu Karb, or Abu Harb, told us on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr that his father advised him, saying: My sons, when I die, wash me. He washed me with water, then dried me in a garment, then washed me the second time with Qarah water, then dried me in a garment, then when I dressed you Clothes, so cover me up."
11019,"(11019) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He should wash his first bath with water of water. The second with water and Sidr, and the third with water and camphor, then the camphor is taken and placed on the places of the mosques."
11020,"(11020) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, he said: Abu Qalab used to wash himself. The dead person was ordered to cover the Sidr, and it was strained in a garment, washed with its strain, and thrown away with its dregs."
11021,"(11021) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai, on the authority of Ubayy, who said, “When Adam became burdensome, he commanded With the intention of finding some of the fruits of Paradise, they came and the angels met them and said: Return, for God has commanded the arrest of your father. So they returned with them, took his soul, and brought with him his shroud and embalmed him, and said to his sons: Bring us, and wash him. They shrouded him, embalmed him, and prayed over him, then said: O children of Adam, this is your practice among yourselves. (Hakim 334)"
11022,"(11022) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir Al-Ahmasi, who said: When Al-Ash’ath died Ibn Qais, and his daughter was the wife of Al-Hasan Ibn Ali. He said: Al-Hasan Ibn Ali said: If you wash him, do not irritate him until You call me to prayer, so We called him out, so he came and performed ablution with spices."
